rigen Navigationsebene Q4 Internship Flash Meet & Greet LMU Karriereforum Working here & abroad: your international career in Bavaria Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal advice Career mentoring Offers for International Students Ambassador Program Internships abroad Cultural & sporting events Our services for employers Privacy policy career events & services User-Support for our portal Application tips for students Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene News and events Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Menu open Menu close You are in the following website hierarchy: Home About LMU LMU at a glance Awards Excellence Strategy University of Excellence Attractive career paths You are here: LMU Research Fellowships LMU Research Fellowships The LMU Research Fellowships are directed at outstanding postdoctoral researchers from all fields of research. Since 2017, the Program has been supported by the European Commission’s Marie Skłodowska-Curie COFUND Action. Supported by an LMU professor, fellows carry out their own two-year research project and thus sharpen their academic profile. Mobility and networking with international partner institutions are particularly promoted through research stays or collaborations. In addition to Incoming Fellowships for outstanding international early-career researchers. LMU also awards Outgoing Fellowships for excellent postdoctoral researchers who have completed their doctorates in the last twelve months or are about to do so. The LMU Research Fellows are members of the Young Center of the LMU Center for Advanced Studies . Since the start of the LMU Research Fellowship Program in 2009, a total of 74 excellent junior academics have been funded in eight calls, 46 of whom came from institutions abroad, 45 percent were women. Almost all former fellows remained in academia and subsequently obtained attractive positions at renowned academic institutions, including professorships at institutions such as the University of Oxford, New York University, and EPF Lausanne. No further calls are planned at this time. Selected success stories News Getting to Grips with Clouds Read more Meteorologist Linda Forster is an Outgoing LMU Research Fellow engaged on a project on cloud formation at the California Institute of Technology (Caltech) and at LMU Munich. The results may help predict future climate change. News Travel broadens the mind Read more Chemist Henry Schurkus is the first Outgoing LMU Fellow. As part of his Fellowship, he worked at the California Institute of Technology in Pasadena. His project could help to make hydrogen production more carbon-neutral. News Object lessons Read more Art historian Philippe Cordez extracts hidden connotations from objects preserved from pre-modern times. He joined LMU as a Research Fellow and subsequently headed a Junior Research Group funded by the Elite Network of Bavaria. Contact Patricia Frohberg Research Strategy Unit Coordinator LMU Research Fellowships Send an email +49 89 2180-3702 More This project has received funding from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 Research and Innovation Programme under the Marie Skłodowska-Curie Grant Agreement No. 754388. up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close Schließen"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/about-lmu/international-network/lmu-stellenbosch-university-su-research-cooperation-program/": {
      "title": "LMU-Stellenbosch University (SU) Research Cooperation Program",
      "description": "LMU-Stellenbosch University (SU) Research Cooperation Program - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search The navigation is not working right now! We work on it. Please use the Sitemap to navigate the website. You are in the following website hierarchy: Home About LMU International network You are here: LMU-Stellenbosch University (SU) Research Cooperation Program LMU-Stellenbosch University (SU) Research Cooperation Program The LMU-SU Research Cooperation Program was established in 2025 to promote and support research collaboration between LMU Munich and Stellenbosch University (SU). Enlarge The LMU-SU partnership is open to all disciplines and supports joint research and partnership development projects, workshops, conferences, as well as mobility opportunities for early-career researchers and professors. Call for Applications For the 2027 funding period , researchers from LMU and Stellenbosch University are invited to submit joint applications for funding within the LMU–SU Research Cooperation Program. Funding is available for joint research activities, including research projects, workshops and conferences, as well as individual mobility. Applications may request funding of up to €25,000 for the funding period from January 1 to December 31, 2027 . Eligible applicants are researchers holding a doctoral degree who are employed at LMU or Stellenbosch University. Doctoral candidates are not eligible to apply as Principal Investigators (PIs) but are expressly encouraged to participate in the projects. The application process for the 2027 funding period is expected to open in September 2026. Further information on the call and application process will be published on this website in the coming weeks. LMU–SU Networking Week An LMU–SU Networking Week is held annually as part of the funded research projects. The event brings together funded researchers from different disciplines and is hosted alternately by LMU and Stellenbosch University. It aims to promote interdisciplinary and international exchange , strengthen connections among the funded projects, and generate new ideas and opportunities for further collaboration. Impressions from the LMU–SU Networking Week 2026 are available in the video. 28 Aug 2026 Information on Further Funding Opportunities In addition to funding available through the LMU–SU Research Cooperation Program , researchers may consider BayIntAn – Promoting Cooperation , a funding program of the Bavarian Research Alliance (BayFOR) that supports the development of international research collaborations. Within the framework of this initial funding for international research cooperation, eligible travel expenses of up to €10,000 may be reimbursed. Further information on the funding conditions and application process is available on the Bavarian Research Alliance website . For further information or questions, please contact the LMU International Office at network.international@lmu.de or the academic coordinator, Prof. Dr. Alexandra Kertz-Welzel. Academic Coordinators Universität Stellenbosch: Prof. Herman Wasserman LMU München: Prof. Dr. Alexandra Kertz-Welzel Contact Program Coordination Stellenbosch University: Sarah van der Westhuizen via sarahvdw@sun.ac.za LMU Munich: Hannah Weckemann via network.international@lmu.de up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close Schließen"
    },
