el Gain experience abroad Overview: Gain experience abroad Internships abroad 6 Sub-items at the next level Internships abroad Overview: Internships abroad Finding an internship abroad 2 Sub-items at the next level Finding an internship abroad Overview: Finding an internship abroad Travel and safety information Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Scholarships 5 Sub-items at the next level Scholarships Overview: Scholarships Erasmus+ Traineeship Programme Career Service Scholarship PROMOS LMU Additional scholarships Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal stories Internships abroad Online Job Portals for International Internships Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Career Services 14 Sub-items at the next level Career Services Overview: Career Services Partner Companies Job portal 2 Sub-items at the next level Job portal Overview: Job portal Manual Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Career and networking events 10 Sub-items at the next level Career and networking events Overview: Career and networking events Career Talk Career Marathon Meet & Greet - Learn & Apply Career Trek Workshops and Seminars 8 Sub-items at the next level Workshops and Seminars Overview: Workshops and Seminars Seminars for acquiring soft skills and application-relevant knowledge Knowledge relevant to job applications and careers Subject-specific courses Microsoft Certificate AI & IT-Security Business administration and then finally weekend! Seminars for International Students Business language courses Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Q4 Internship Flash Meet & Greet LMU Karriereforum Working here & abroad: your international career in Bavaria Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal advice Career mentoring Offers for International Students Ambassador Program Internships abroad Cultural & sporting events Our services for employers Privacy policy career events & services User-Support for our portal Application tips for students Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene News and events Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Menu open Menu close You are in the following website hierarchy: Home About LMU Working at LMU Academic Careers Pathways to LMU The doctoral phase You are here: Find your topic Find your topic Your doctoral thesis is the first contribution to your field of research, and lays the foundations for your subsequent career in academia. That's why it's so important to choose the right topic. It should be more than simply a topic that's relevant to the academic field — it should concern something you feel passionate about! Skip to content Conditions How do I find the right topic for me? Interesting links Conditions Following completion of a State Examination ( Staatsexamen ), Diplom (German academic degree), Magister (German academic degree) or master's degree, candidates can apply for a doctoral degree. Promotionsordnung (doctoral degree regulations) for each subject determine who is eligible. In most cases, above-average academic performance in the preceding degree program is a prerequisite for acceptance to becoming a doctoral candidate. The core component in doctoral studies is the independent preparation of an extensive academic research paper (dissertation), which must be published. In addition, some subjects require successful candidates to fulfill further requirements. Doctoral studies conclude with a comprehensive final examination (\"Rigorosum\") or a so-called Disputation , in which each doctoral candidate presents their doctoral thesis to the public and engages in a specialist discussion with university lecturers. How do I find the right topic for me? If you're thinking about your dissertation, you're probably working on your master's degree right now. As a first step, consider the field you're interested in and, based on that, define your desired research direction. Read the most recent literature and identify an issue that you feel has not been adequately addressed within the academic world. As a second step, you should identify eligible doctoral supervisors, whose research profile and interests fit your project idea. An alternative approach is to contact the appropriate institute in your faculty . It can also be useful to look at advertisements for doctoral positions or for structured doctoral programs . In the natural and life sciences, specific doctoral topics are often advertised, especially if the position is part of an externally funded project. You can find these either directly on each institution's website or on the LMU job portal . Once you have decided on a potential supervisor, you can contact them directly. If you have reached an agreement with your future supervisor or have been accepted into a structured doctoral program, you are ready to let yourself be accepted as a doctoral candidate in the faculty concerned. Interesting links Individual doctoral studies Structured doctoral programs LMU faculties Guide to applying for doctoral studies Registration for doctoral studies up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München