ational Student Guide Overview: International Student Guide Checklists Health and safety Visa Registering your address Residence permit Opening a bank account Living costs Academic culture Working in Germany Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Student support services 8 Sub-items at the next level Student support services Overview: Student support services Finance your studies 2 Sub-items at the next level Finance your studies Overview: Finance your studies Scholarships 5 Sub-items at the next level Scholarships Overview: Scholarships Deutschlandstipendium 3 Sub-items at the next level Deutschlandstipendium Overview: Deutschlandstipendium Application Events Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Grants from foundation funds Oskar Karl Forster Scholarship Scholarships for international students Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Studying with a child 2 Sub-items at the next level Studying with a child Overview: Studying with a child International student parents Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Studying with a disability 6 Sub-items at the next level Studying with a disability Overview: Studying with a disability Advice and networking Special applications Compensation for disadvantages Barrier-free access and aids FAQs Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Studying in the first generation Workshops on study skills and co. IT service offers Peer support Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Gain experience abroad 2 Sub-items at the next level Gain experience abroad Overview: Gain experience abroad Internships abroad 6 Sub-items at the next level Internships abroad Overview: Internships abroad Finding an internship abroad 2 Sub-items at the next level Finding an internship abroad Overview: Finding an internship abroad Travel and safety information Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Scholarships 5 Sub-items at the next level Scholarships Overview: Scholarships Erasmus+ Traineeship Programme Career Service Scholarship PROMOS LMU Additional scholarships Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal stories Internships abroad Online Job Portals for International Internships Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Career Services 14 Sub-items at the next level Career Services Overview: Career Services Partner Companies Job portal 2 Sub-items at the next level Job portal Overview: Job portal Manual Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Career and networking events 10 Sub-items at the next level Career and networking events Overview: Career and networking events Career Talk Career Marathon Meet & Greet - Learn & Apply Career Trek Workshops and Seminars 8 Sub-items at the next level Workshops and Seminars Overview: Workshops and Seminars Seminars for acquiring soft skills and application-relevant knowledge Knowledge relevant to job applications and careers Subject-specific courses Microsoft Certificate AI & IT-Security Business administration and then finally weekend! Seminars for International Students Business language courses Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Q4 Internship Flash Meet & Greet LMU Karriereforum Working here & abroad: your international career in Bavaria Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal advice Career mentoring Offers for International Students Ambassador Program Internships abroad Cultural & sporting events Our services for employers Privacy policy career events & services User-Support for our portal Application tips for students Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene News and events Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Menu open Menu close You are in the following website hierarchy: Home About LMU Working at LMU Academic Careers You are here: Funding opportunities Funding opportunities at LMU Shape your career by getting the right help from the start! LMU offers perfect research and career development conditions, spanning all phases of your academic journey — from doctorate to professorship. The LMU Academic Career Program provides outstanding junior researchers with ideal research and qualification conditions. At every career stage - from doctorate to postdoc to tenure track and finally to lifetime professorship - LMU offers a wide range of interdisciplinary and subject-specific funding opportunities and services to support you in developing your scientific independence and a competitive research profile, in networking both within and outside academia, and in balancing career and family. Funding opportunities for the career phase you're in Change content The doctoral phase The postdoc phase The tenure-track phase The doctoral phase During your doctoral phase, LMU is here to champion your academic qualification, professional development and career planning. Information on support services for doctoral candidates is provided by the LMU Graduate Center — the central coordination, advisory and service facility for doctoral studies at LMU . Subject-specific funding opportunities can be found on the sites of our faculties , collaborative research projects , and doctoral programs . The postdoc phase Whether you're on the road to a professorship or pursuing a career outside of academia, LMU supports you in your postdoctoral phase to get your career well planned out. We do this by helping you broaden your international horizons and establish yourself as an independent researcher through networking and mobility. Research: The Junior Researcher Fund promotes the individual career development of junior academics (who have gained no more than six years of professional academic experience since having completed their doctorate) by providing support for the independent procurement of externally funded and peer-reviewed research projects, particularly of prestigious research prizes and awards directed at junior academics. Through the Junior Researchers in Residence program, the Center for Advanced Studies (CAS) offers outstanding junior academics an attractive opportunity to conduct intensive research on a single topic for one full semester. The CAS Young Center comprises outstanding LMU junior academics, including holders of renowned awards and scholarships. The Postdoc Support Fund provides additional resources to LMU’s individual faculties to facilitate flexible, subject-specific promotion of postdoctoral researchers, particularly for the recruitment of international postdocs, to facilitate the continuation of scientific activity, e.g. following periods of parental leave (re-entry funding), for networking activities, as well as for open-access publishing activities. Some faculties present their Postdoc Support Fund offers on dedicated websites: Faculty of Catholic Theology Faculty of Protestant Theology Faculty of Economics (integrated in the Junior Development Program) Faculty of Medicine Faculty of History and the Arts: History Department Faculty of History and the Arts: School of the Arts Faculty of Philosophy, Philosophy of Science and Religious Studies Faculty of Languages and Literatures (integrated in the Nachwuchsförderprogramm) Faculty of Social Sciences Faculty of Mathematics, Informatics and Statistics Faculty of Geosciences (integrated in funding@geo) The Knowledge Transfer Fund provides seed funding for projects aimed at the development of basic research into technological, social or economic innovations. Internationalization: Through the Postdoc Support Fund , established as part of the LMU's funding as a University of Excellence, our faculties promote international networking , from conference trips to hosting your own conferences and workshops. Some faculties present their Postdoc Support Fund offers on dedicated websites (see above under „Research“). Harnessing LMU's international network, postdocs are given a number of opportunities to build international networks and take advantage of mobility. This is enabled, for example, via the many strategic partnerships nurtured by LMUexcellent or the Erasmus+ mobility network. Mentoring: Within the scope of the LMU Mentoring program, excellent junior academics can seek career advice from personally selected mentors and receive subject-specific guidance in developing their careers. Publication: The LMU Open Access Fund supports open access publications with a grant towards publication costs. Subject-specific funding opportunities can be found on the sites of our faculties , collaborative research projects , and doctoral programs . The tenure-track phase The Tenure Track Model offers junior academics an early-stage, attractive career path towards a permanent professorship at LMU. Tenure-track professors at LMU can draw on a variety of support in building their academic profile. Research: The Investment Fund provides seed funding for the procurement of large-scale third-party funding projects directed at innovative research ideas and the establishment of new research fields. The Junior Researcher Fund promotes the individual career development of junior academics (who have gained no more than six years of professional academic experience since having completed their doctorate) by providing support for the independent procurement of externally funded and peer-reviewed research projects, particularly of prestigious research prizes and awards directed at junior academics. As a forum for cross-disciplinary academic exchange, the Center for Advanced Studies (CAS) promotes various types of cooperative research and academic exchange. The CAS Young Center comprises outstanding LMU junior academics, including holders of renowned awards and scholarships. Internationalization: By harnessing LMU's international network, there are numerous opportunities to build international networks and take advantage of mobility . This is enabled, for example, via the many strategic partnerships nurtured by LMUexcellent or the Erasmus+ mobility network. Equal opportunities: In order to increase the proportion of women among professors, the Adele  Hartmann Program additionally promotes the appointment of outstanding female researchers to W2 professorships. Publication: The LMU Open Access Fund supports open access publications with a grant towards publication costs. Subject-specific funding opportunities can be found on the sites of our faculties , collaborative research projects , and doctoral programs . Further funding opportunities Funding and support services of the University Women's Representative Funding opportunities by the Munich University Association (in German) Advice on third-party funding programs We are here to share information and advise you when it comes to the requirements and success factors for third-party funded research projects. Research services Information events on funding programs (restricted access) Funding database Pivot-RP (restricted access) At a glance The right support for the postdoc phase (PDF, 96 KB) The right support for the tenure-track phase (PDF, 124 KB) up Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close Schließen"
    },
