ck zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Q4 Internship Flash Meet & Greet LMU Karriereforum Working here & abroad: your international career in Bavaria Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal advice Career mentoring Offers for International Students Ambassador Program Internships abroad Cultural & sporting events Our services for employers Privacy policy career events & services User-Support for our portal Application tips for students Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene News and events Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Menu open Menu close You are in the following website hierarchy: Home About LMU Working at LMU Academic Careers Funding opportunities You are here: STIBET Mentoring Scholarship Program STIBET Mentoring Scholarship Program for international doctoral candidates The STIBET Mentoring Scholarship Program offered by the German Academic Exchange Service (DAAD) supports particularly qualified foreign doctoral candidates. The DAAD has currently suspended the program \"STIBET Doktoranden”. Therefore, no scholarships can be awarded. Further information will be provided here on this webpage as soon as the program is re-opened. Aim Thanks to these resources we can individually support extraordinarily qualified international doctoral students. The aim is to integrate excellent international doctoral candidates into the international activities of their respective department. Scholarship type and objective The International Office awards scholarships for particularly committed doctoral candidates. The aim of these scholarships is to improve support for foreign students and doctoral candidates by having scholarship students take on support tasks or perform other services conducive to international exchange within their faculty. Prerequisites The main prerequisite for funding is the commitment of the scholarship student to promoting the department and support in the supervision of international students, e.g. through social and professional mentoring, language tandems, cooperation in cultural programs, field trips, local interest events, support activities in student housing, and language courses, among others. The decisive criterion for a successful application is a candidate's outstanding academic performance. Applicants who receive funding from the DAAD under another program are not eligible to apply. Application procedure Please fill out the application form (PDF, 99 KB) . In addition, a current resume and two letters of recommendation from your supervising professors must be included. Please email all materials by 15 December to Dr. Dongmei Zhang International Office CSC programs Send an email +49 89 2180-6169 More up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close Schließen"
