tems at the next level Gain experience abroad Overview: Gain experience abroad Internships abroad 6 Sub-items at the next level Internships abroad Overview: Internships abroad Finding an internship abroad 2 Sub-items at the next level Finding an internship abroad Overview: Finding an internship abroad Travel and safety information Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Scholarships 5 Sub-items at the next level Scholarships Overview: Scholarships Erasmus+ Traineeship Programme Career Service Scholarship PROMOS LMU Additional scholarships Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal stories Internships abroad Online Job Portals for International Internships Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Career Services 14 Sub-items at the next level Career Services Overview: Career Services Partner Companies Job portal 2 Sub-items at the next level Job portal Overview: Job portal Manual Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Career and networking events 10 Sub-items at the next level Career and networking events Overview: Career and networking events Career Talk Career Marathon Meet & Greet - Learn & Apply Career Trek Workshops and Seminars 8 Sub-items at the next level Workshops and Seminars Overview: Workshops and Seminars Seminars for acquiring soft skills and application-relevant knowledge Knowledge relevant to job applications and careers Subject-specific courses Microsoft Certificate AI & IT-Security Business administration and then finally weekend! Seminars for International Students Business language courses Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Q4 Internship Flash Meet & Greet LMU Karriereforum Working here & abroad: your international career in Bavaria Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal advice Career mentoring Offers for International Students Ambassador Program Internships abroad Cultural & sporting events Our services for employers Privacy policy career events & services User-Support for our portal Application tips for students Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene News and events Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Menu open Menu close You are in the following website hierarchy: Home About LMU Working at LMU Academic Careers Career options Careers in academia You are here: Professorships and senior positions Professorships and senior positions The successful route to a professorship (or an academic leadership position at a non-university research institution) can follow different paths. Professors are primarily active in research and teaching: conducting research, they continuously expand the knowledge and boundaries of their field, contribute to the development of specific as well as interdisciplinary approaches, and so also drive the formation of new fields within academia. Depending on their career stage, position and personal experience, it may be that their own research activities are increasingly replaced by managing larger research projects and leading other researchers. In courses and lectures, they impart the knowledge of their discipline to students and doctoral candidates and provide them with insights into the latest state of research. University professors have a teaching load of eight to nine semester hours per week, depending on the federal state; at universities of applied sciences it can be considerably more. In addition, a professorship includes committee activities, the supervision of junior academics and the transfer of knowledge. Subject-related and methodological qualification Qualification and personal development Read more A professorship involves a range of responsibilities that are very diverse and extensive. No wonder the requirements profile is correspondingly demanding: In the foreground of course — is the candidate's academic, subject-related and methodological qualification, which must be demonstrated through \"additional academic achievements\" following their degree program and doctoral studies. There are many ways to achieve this in the German academic system: a junior professorship; leading your own independent junior research group; or the German Habilitation (post-doctoral qualification) which is still required in some subjects and can be carried out in a variety of positions — to name just a few examples. International networking and success in acquiring third-party funding also play a major role in an appointment to a professorship. In addition, there are didactic skills and competencies in the areas of communication and cooperation, leadership and management, as well as self-management and career development. LMU Tenure Track Model Detailed information on the LMU Tenure Track Model Read more For young academics, the tenure-track professorship offers a particularly attractive and reliable path: although the appointment is initially limited in time, the tenure-track phase leads directly to a permanent professorship, following a positive evaluation. LMU introduced its Tenure Track Model more than ten years ago and has continued to develop it ever since. The aim of this model is, early on, to lay out an attractive career path for junior academics that leads to a permanent professorship at LMU. Currently, more than 200 academics are on the tenure track under this model, or have already completed it. Career options on the path to professorships and senior positions Career advice for postdocs (restricted access) Read more Once appointed to a professorship, further opportunities for development still exist: Specifically, the German civil service remuneration system differentiates between W1 or junior professorships, W2 and W3 professorships. Here, the \"W\" stands for the academic remuneration scale stipulated in the Federal Civil Service Remuneration Regulation ( Bundesbesoldungs ordnung ). The basic salary and further structuring of a professorship differs significantly depending on the German federal state and university in question. However, as a general rule, the chance to negotiate both the basic salary and additional benefits associated with performance and facilities increases at higher appointment levels. Senior positions are also available at numerous non-university research institutes, such as those of the Max Planck Society, the Helmholtz Association and the Fraunhofer Society. Since directors of these institutions are often also appointed to a university at the same time, there is considerable overlap with the requirements for a professorship. In addition, each research institution has its own specific research profile, which stipulates additional focal points for its academic management. At LMU, you will have the opportunity to reflect on your competencies and development goals in our career advice sessions. This will help you decide whether you want to pursue the career path to a professorship or academic senior position. Moments of choice - The professor If you click to view this video your personal data will be transmitted to YouTube and cookies may also be stored on your device. LMU has no influence over how any such data is transmitted or indeed over its further usage. More information available here: LMU data protection policy , data protection policy from YouTube / Google I acknowledge that I have read and understood the information concerning the protection of my data and am willing to display the embedded content despite potential risks. 05:09\n\t\t\t\t        \t\t | \n\t\t\t\t\t        \t18 Jan 2023\n\t\t\t\t        \t\t |  \n\t\t\t\t        \t\t\t©LMU Scientists can find subject-specific information on career-relevant topics on the websites of the faculties , collaborative research projects , and doctoral programs . LMU academics can find access-protected detailed descriptions of our services in the Service Portal . These include names of current contact people and the relevant application forms. Interesting links Find an open      position on LMU's \"Stellenportal\" (in German) Information on the authorization to teach (venia legendi) at the University (restricted access) Contact Career advice for postdocs Elisabethplatz 22 80796 München Directions (https://maps.app.goo.gl/sawNuPPZZvr2tYUh8) research-careers@Verwaltung.Uni-Muenchen.de Send an email +49 89 2180-72287 up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close Schließen"
