 level Gain experience abroad Overview: Gain experience abroad Internships abroad 6 Sub-items at the next level Internships abroad Overview: Internships abroad Finding an internship abroad 2 Sub-items at the next level Finding an internship abroad Overview: Finding an internship abroad Travel and safety information Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Scholarships 5 Sub-items at the next level Scholarships Overview: Scholarships Erasmus+ Traineeship Programme Career Service Scholarship PROMOS LMU Additional scholarships Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal stories Internships abroad Online Job Portals for International Internships Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Career Services 14 Sub-items at the next level Career Services Overview: Career Services Partner Companies Job portal 2 Sub-items at the next level Job portal Overview: Job portal Manual Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Career and networking events 10 Sub-items at the next level Career and networking events Overview: Career and networking events Career Talk Career Marathon Meet & Greet - Learn & Apply Career Trek Workshops and Seminars 8 Sub-items at the next level Workshops and Seminars Overview: Workshops and Seminars Seminars for acquiring soft skills and application-relevant knowledge Knowledge relevant to job applications and careers Subject-specific courses Microsoft Certificate AI & IT-Security Business administration and then finally weekend! Seminars for International Students Business language courses Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Q4 Internship Flash Meet & Greet LMU Karriereforum Working here & abroad: your international career in Bavaria Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal advice Career mentoring Offers for International Students Ambassador Program Internships abroad Cultural & sporting events Our services for employers Privacy policy career events & services User-Support for our portal Application tips for students Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene News and events Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Menu open Menu close You are in the following website hierarchy: Home About LMU Working at LMU Academic Careers Career options Career paths outside academia You are here: Careers in business A career in business — but how? Whether you are specifically looking for a job in business or beyond, you want to explore alternatives to a university career early on, or are still undecided — you can find information on possible careers outside of academia here. The doctorate — a core qualification for the labor market Advice for doctoral candidates Read more In Germany, only about 15 percent of all doctoral graduates are employed at universities; and about half leave academia immediately following their doctorate . Attractive positions are available in all areas — from business and industry to insurance and banking, politics (political consulting) and non-governmental organizations, health care and public administration, educational institutions and training providers, the media sector and cultural institutions. Doctoral graduates bring with them competences that are in high demand in the non-academic job market: In addition to their ability to work in detail on a complex subject, they have demonstrated personal responsibility, perseverance and the ability to find solutions. They have learned to present complex issues in a clear and comprehensible manner and have suitable presentation and visualization techniques. In addition, working in mixed and often international teams, has trained their communication and cooperation skills. In some cases, initial leadership experience can also be demonstrated, e.g. in supervising student assistants and later in the postdoc phase of doctoral candidates. Career options outside of academia Career advice for postdocs (restricted access) Read more It's important to understand what's on offer in the world outside academia, as well as know your own strengths and priorities, in order to make a successful transition to the business world. At LMU, you will have the opportunity to reflect on your personal strengths, work experience, and development goals in one of our career advice sessions. This should help you to decide whether you would like to pursue a career path outside of academia and what the next steps might be. LMU qualification opportunities Qualification and personal development Read more LMU also supports you when it comes to building your career-relevant competences by offering a versatile range of qualification and developmental opportunities. In doing so, we also focus on areas of development that can be relevant for careers outside of academia: Competences in communication and cooperation, but also leadership and management as well self-management and career planning. Self-employment With a promising business idea, the dream of owning your own company can become a reality. Good preparation is crucial for a start-up — from that first business plan to financing. With a comprehensive range of services, — from events and workshops to specific practical training, start-up advice and support in obtaining funding — LMU promotes entrepreneurial thinking and doing among its young academics. Moments of Choice - The entrepreneur If you click to view this video your personal data will be transmitted to YouTube and cookies may also be stored on your device. LMU has no influence over how any such data is transmitted or indeed over its further usage. More information available here: LMU data protection policy , data protection policy from YouTube / Google I acknowledge that I have read and understood the information concerning the protection of my data and am willing to display the embedded content despite potential risks. 03:37\n\t\t\t\t        \t\t | \n\t\t\t\t\t        \t1 Feb 2023\n\t\t\t\t        \t\t |  \n\t\t\t\t        \t\t\t©LMU Interesting links University-related startups (LMU Spin-off Service) LMU Innovation & Entrepreneurship Center Information on career opportunities for humanities graduates (in German) Contact Advice for doctoral candidates Elisabethplatz 22 80796 München Directions (https://maps.app.goo.gl/sawNuPPZZvr2tYUh8) graduatecenter@lmu.de Send an email +49 89 2180-9731 Career advice for postdocs Elisabethplatz 22 80796 München Directions (https://maps.app.goo.gl/sawNuPPZZvr2tYUh8) research-careers@Verwaltung.Uni-Muenchen.de Send an email +49 89 2180-72287 Spin-off Service Elisabethplatz 22 80796 München Directions (https://maps.app.goo.gl/sawNuPPZZvr2tYUh8) spinoffservice@lmu.de Send an email +49 89 2180-72233 up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close Schließen"
