nternational Student Guide Overview: International Student Guide Checklists Health and safety Visa Registering your address Residence permit Opening a bank account Living costs Academic culture Working in Germany Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Student support services 8 Sub-items at the next level Student support services Overview: Student support services Finance your studies 2 Sub-items at the next level Finance your studies Overview: Finance your studies Scholarships 5 Sub-items at the next level Scholarships Overview: Scholarships Deutschlandstipendium 3 Sub-items at the next level Deutschlandstipendium Overview: Deutschlandstipendium Application Events Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Grants from foundation funds Oskar Karl Forster Scholarship Scholarships for international students Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Studying with a child 2 Sub-items at the next level Studying with a child Overview: Studying with a child International student parents Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Studying with a disability 6 Sub-items at the next level Studying with a disability Overview: Studying with a disability Advice and networking Special applications Compensation for disadvantages Barrier-free access and aids FAQs Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Studying in the first generation Workshops on study skills and co. IT service offers Peer support Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Gain experience abroad 2 Sub-items at the next level Gain experience abroad Overview: Gain experience abroad Internships abroad 6 Sub-items at the next level Internships abroad Overview: Internships abroad Finding an internship abroad 2 Sub-items at the next level Finding an internship abroad Overview: Finding an internship abroad Travel and safety information Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Scholarships 5 Sub-items at the next level Scholarships Overview: Scholarships Erasmus+ Traineeship Programme Career Service Scholarship PROMOS LMU Additional scholarships Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal stories Internships abroad Online Job Portals for International Internships Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Career Services 14 Sub-items at the next level Career Services Overview: Career Services Partner Companies Job portal 2 Sub-items at the next level Job portal Overview: Job portal Manual Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Career and networking events 10 Sub-items at the next level Career and networking events Overview: Career and networking events Career Talk Career Marathon Meet & Greet - Learn & Apply Career Trek Workshops and Seminars 8 Sub-items at the next level Workshops and Seminars Overview: Workshops and Seminars Seminars for acquiring soft skills and application-relevant knowledge Knowledge relevant to job applications and careers Subject-specific courses Microsoft Certificate AI & IT-Security Business administration and then finally weekend! Seminars for International Students Business language courses Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Q4 Internship Flash Meet & Greet LMU Karriereforum Working here & abroad: your international career in Bavaria Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal advice Career mentoring Offers for International Students Ambassador Program Internships abroad Cultural & sporting events Our services for employers Privacy policy career events & services User-Support for our portal Application tips for students Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene News and events Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Menu open Menu close You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Gain experience abroad Internships abroad Scholarships You are here: Career Service Scholarship Career Services Scholarship Do you want to do a short internship in another European country and don't know how to finance it? LMU Career Services offers financial support to students registered at LMU. Skip to content Grant requirements Scholarship Process Contact Grant requirements Who can apply? To apply for the Career Services Scholarship, you must meet the following requirements: Internship is in another European country (but not in your own home country) You are registered at LMU You may not have a permanent residence in the internship country. Registration there is only allowed for the internship duration. Which internships are eligible? Full-time internships of 30 hours or more per week or 12 hours of instruction per week for teaching internships. Voluntary and mandatory internships Types of internships: Regular internships at all kinds of institutions (companies, NGOs, hospitals, etc.) Teaching internships at foreign schools Paid (up to 1000 euros/month) and unpaid internships Relevant to your degree program Internship duration of at least 53 to a maximum of 59 days. Please check the length of your internship. The Erasmus+ Programme usually funds longer internships. Scholarship Process 1. Basic details You got accepted for your dream internship? Great! Please email the following information to LMU Career Services to start your scholarship application: Exact date of the beginning of your internship (e.g. Monday, the...) Exact date of the end of the internship (e.g. Friday, the...) Location of your internship Country of your internship Your faculty at LMU (number and name) Name of the your internship institution Scholarship: Career Services Scholarship After this, you'll receive a link to the application portal from us. Without these basic details we can't process your application! 2. Your application Application deadline : latest four weeks before the start of your internship! Please apply through the MoveON portal. To use this, you have to register with your LMU email address. Please select the online form \"Bewerbung Stipendium Auslandspraktikum\" (Scholarship Application for Internships Abroad) in the portal. The following documents must be uploaded to apply for the Career Services Scholarship: A Placement Offer (DOC, 92 KB) signed by your internship provider In addition to conventional wet signatures, we also accept digital signatures , provided that the handwriting of the respective person is recognizable. Documents can therefore be signed on a tablet, for example. Letter of motivation (1 – 2 pages) Resume Registration certificate If required, proof of participation in a training course on intercultural competence Insurance declaration (PDF, 52 KB) What happens after I have handed in my application? Once we've received all of the documents listed above, the first scholarship installment will be disbursed. 3. Selection process Scholarships are awarded in the order in which we receive complete applications via MoveON. The decisive point here is the submission of your complete application via MoveON, not the basic details that you send via e-mail. Please check your application thoroughly before submitting it. If we find any discrepancies upon reviewing it, you will have the opportunity to correct your information after your application is reactivated by us. Scholarship applications will be rejected if they do not meet the criteria listed on this website or if we no longer have funding available 4. Changes during your internship If the time frame of your internship changes, it is necessary to submit a new Placement Offer. Furterhmore, your Internship Certificate for the final documents has to show the updated duration of your stay. 5. After your placement Internship certificate , which is issued by your employer and includes the beginning and ending dates of your internship. Reimbursement of travel expenses : Please make sure you only depart home after the last day of your internship. Internship report (DOC, 143 KB) , which - upon your approval - we will anonymise and upload to our website containing personal stories and institutions. Your registration certificate — if the confirmation submitted with your application doesn't cover the entire period of your internship. Career tip : Your internship provider can issue a qualified reference for you. This reference looks great in future applications! Please upload all final documents in one go to the MoveON portal no later than 30 days after concluding your internship. You will have already received the link to this portal with your application. Contact Do you have any further questions on this program? Then you're welcome to contact us for a consultation! Team Auslandspraktika LMU's Career Services Your contact for the planning and organization of internships abroad, incl. scholarship applications Send an email More up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close Schließen"
    },
