ionsebene Q4 Internship Flash Meet & Greet LMU Karriereforum Working here & abroad: your international career in Bavaria Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal advice Career mentoring Offers for International Students Ambassador Program Internships abroad Cultural & sporting events Our services for employers Privacy policy career events & services User-Support for our portal Application tips for students Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene News and events Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Menu open Menu close You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services Career and networking events You are here: Career Talk LMU Career Talk 2026 The LMU Career Talk is the annual highlight for all those who want to actively shape their professional future. Every year we focus on a new, highly topical career topic that will shape the working world of tomorrow. LMU Career Talk on July 10, 2026 Enlarge High school graduation, college, dream job! — Everything's going according to plan... right? Look forward to an inspiring panel discussion in the morning, where renowned experts from various industries will share exciting insights and practical tips on the latest career trends. Let the experiences and stories of successful professionals motivate you and discover new perspectives for your own career. Moderator: Lothar Wüst - Managing Director, Cormens Anne Brier – Director of the Mentoring Program at the Munich Press Club / Journalist for Bayerischer Rundfunk, among others Dr. Markus Gruber – Director General, Bavarian State Ministry of Family, Labor, and Social Affairs Pascal Heß – Labor Market Economist at the IAB (Institute for Employment Research) Eva Kraatz – Coach and Trainer—including for the LMU mentors / long-time mentor Elke Pfnür – HVB Unicredit Germany – Archivist & Historian at the Bank Alexander Vocelka - Senior AI Advisor - ThinkaDo Following that, and in preparation for the networking lunch buffet: World Café on the Topic: Career Instead of Knockout in the Age of AI Moderator: Dr. Stephan Pflaum The afternoon is all about networking : Here, students from all disciplines have a unique opportunity to make valuable connections and exchange ideas across industries. Take this chance to learn from your fellow students’ experiences, make new friends, and expand your professional network. The LMU Career Talk is more than just an event—it’s your springboard to a successful future. Join us and take an active role in shaping your career! Participating companies: ADAC Basycon Bavarian State Ministry of Family, Labor, and Social Affairs FTAPI Goethe-Institut HypoVereinsbank - UniCredit Germany IAB - Institute for Employment Research innoscripta City of Munich, IT Department SwissRe Press Club SIXT ThinkaDo The event will take place at the Kardinal-Wendel-Haus in Munich. Schedule Time Program item starting at 8:30 a.m. Check-In 9:00 a.m. Main Hall, Ground Floor Opening Remarks: Dr. Markus Gruber, Director General of the Bavarian State Ministry of Family, Labor, and Social Affairs Opening Remarks: Dr. Margit Weber, Vice President for Equal Opportunity, Talent Development, and Diversity 9:15 a.m. – 11:45 a.m. Main Hall, Ground Floor Panel discussion with renowned experts (see above) . Followed by a World Café on the topic \" Career Instead of Knockout in the Age of AI\" 12:00 p.m. – 1:30 p.m. Lunch & Networking Area (near the Great Hall and in the palace gardens) Networking Lunch 12:30 p.m. – 4:00 p.m. Main Hall, Ground Floor Smart Job Fair & Keynotes Resume Reviews at the FTAPI Booth 1:00 p.m. – 2:30 p.m. Library, 1st Floor Keynote: AI in Your Career! Have the Courage to Use It! - Viola Kraus ( Pre-registration required ) 2:30 p.m. – 5:30 p.m. Library, 1st Floor Workshop: Have the Courage to Pursue a Career! Have the Courage to Make Decisions! - Anne Brier ( Pre-registration required ) 2:00 p.m. – 6:00 p.m. Conference Room, 1st Floor Workshop: AI & Career @ Career Talk, Beginner-Friendly Workshop with the LRZ ( Pre-registration required ) around 4:15 p.m. End of the event Impressions 2025 & 2024 1 of 6 Previous Next Dr.phil. Stephan Pflaum LMU's Career Services Consultant Career Events & Services / Deputy Head of Career Service Send an email Zoom appointment for employers More Dirk Erfurth LMU's Career Services Head of Career Service / Business Coach Advanced Send an email More Johanna Uitz, M.A. LMU's Career Services Consultant for Internationalization & Employability / project manager FIT-LMU International Careers, Events & Seminars, Mentoring, Employer Services Send an email More up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close Schließen"
