rachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Q4 Internship Flash Meet & Greet LMU Karriereforum Working here & abroad: your international career in Bavaria Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal advice Career mentoring Offers for International Students Ambassador Program Internships abroad Cultural & sporting events Our services for employers Privacy policy career events & services User-Support for our portal Application tips for students Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene News and events Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Menu open Menu close You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services Career and networking events Workshops and Seminars You are here: Knowledge relevant to job applications and careers Seminars relevant to job applications and careers Skip to content 09.09. Future of Work - AI and Career 23.09. How do I present myself at a job interview? 14.10. Career decisions made easy 21.10. Strategic and effective Jobsearch 28.10. Preparation for job interviews, telephone and online interviews 18.11. Business Knigge 25.11. Application Workshop for International Students 02.12. Assessment center: The supreme discipline among selection procedures 09.12. Rights and obligations at work in Germany: employment contract, salaries, references 16.12. LinkedIn workshop \"How To Use LinkedIn\" Show more 09.09. Future of Work - AI and Career Anmeldung Read more 09.09.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 - online (Zoom) - max 20 participants - Language: English - Trainer: Viola Kraus \"Future of Work - How the topic of (generative) AI will challenge us now and in the future and how we can learn to deal with it in order to make use of it\" Everyone is talking about AI, generative AI (GenAI). Companies want to use it in a targeted manner and some of us are asking ourselves \"what do I need to know, what else should I learn\". As an active member of our society, as future employees and teachers, we can prepare ourselves for these complex questions and the unknown. What should we already know and what can we still learn? Which gadgets can be used where and how, and are they used by companies? What unknowns are we likely to have to deal with? And what contribution can each of us make to society? 23.09. How do I present myself at a job interview? Anmeldung Read more 23.09.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 Uhr - Hansa Haus München (Läugerzimmer) - max 20 TN - Sprache: Englisch - Trainerin: Eva Kraatz In this workshop you will get a good understanding of how to prepare for a job interview. The following topics will be covered: General preparation for your job interview: Company and market environment About me (skills, questions, expectations, how I fit in with the company, etc.) Basic information on interview situations and more 14.10. Career decisions made easy Anmeldung Read more 14.10.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 - Hansa Haus München (Läugerzimmer) - max. 20 participants - Language: German - Trainer: Eva Kraatz What do I do after university? Which job, which professional environment suits me best? What exactly do I want? There are so many options, which one is right for me? It is not always easy to decide which career path to take after graduation. In this seminar, we will look at our personal values, among other things, as these have a decisive influence on our lives - albeit often unconsciously. If we know our values, we can not only make suitable but also sustainable professional or career decisions. The afternoon will be rounded off with various tips and tricks for general decision-making. In this workshop we will work on the following topics: Personal values Hierarchy of personal values Tips & tricks for decision-making ...and even more... 21.10. Strategic and effective Jobsearch Anmeldung Read more 21.10.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 Uhr - Hansa Haus München (Läugerzimmer) - max 20 TN - Sprache: Englisch - Trainerin: Heike Anne Dietzel - Karrierecoach Searching for a new job can be a very time-consuming and long effort: there are hundreds of job search engines, matching portals and companies post their vacancies on Social media. What is the most effective way to find a new job? Get a glimpse behind the scenes of the recruiting process Build your application strategy that matches your background, personality and interests Understand the variety and evaluate job search channels for your needs Do’s and Dont’s for your communication with Hiring Managers and Recruiters during your job search Define effective networking channels for job search 28.10. Preparation for job interviews, telephone and online interviews Anmeldung Read more 28.10.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 - Hansa Haus München (Läugerzimmer) - max. 20 participants - Language: German - Trainer: Heike Anne Dietzel - Career coach A job interview can be conducted in very different ways and is always a major challenge. That's why preparation is a central key to being successful in a job interview. Personnel selection: What criteria are used to evaluate an applicant? Different types of job interviews How can I score points as an applicant in a job interview? Self-presentation as an important key to success in an interview Personal branding: positive self-marketing techniques How do I convince people in a conversation and what role does my body language play? Classic, provocative questions and inadmissible questions The most important do's and don'ts for telephone and online interviews 18.11. Business Knigge Anmeldung Read more 18.11.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 Uhr - Hansa Haus München (Läugerzimmer) - max 20 TN - Sprache: Deutsch - Trainer: Isabelle Krier / Eric Fritzsche Immer da, wo Menschen aufeinander treffen gibt es Regeln für den Umgangs miteinander. Manche davon werden offen ausgesprochen, andere sind „ungeschriebene Gesetze“. Auf jeden Fall wird das neue Umfeld ungewohnt sein. Je mehr jedoch darüber bekannt ist, desto selbstsicherer wird dein Auftreten als Berufsanfänger:in sein. Das gilt für ein Praktikum, den Werkstudenten-Job oder die erste „richtige“ Stelle. In diesem Workshop lernst du ein paar einfache Regeln, wir erkunden gemeinsam den Weg durch den „Business Dschungel“ und wir verhelfen dir zu einem gesunden Maß an Selbstsicherheit für einen guten Start. Inhalte: Was sind die typischen Fettnäpfchen? Gibt es (noch) eine Kleiderordnung? Einfluss der Unternehmenskultur auf das Miteinander Der Alltag im Büroleben/Home-Office/Business-Meetings, worauf muss ich achten? Umgang mit Social Media – während und nach der Arbeit Firmenfeiern Geschäftsessen und vieles mehr 25.11. Application Workshop for International Students Anmeldung Read more 25.11.2024 - 10:00 - 16:00 - live&local - Hansa Haus München (Saal) - max. 20 participants - language: English - Trainer: Janine Müller Other countries, other manners - applying for your first job in Germany Getting started for your first job in Germany can be irritating. We will give you a good overview about the way to apply for a job in Germany among the candidate lifecycle: How to read job advertisements? What to prepare for the formal application? How can you prepare yourself for the job interview to make a great first impression? What is necessary to know for you first day and the onboarding period? ...and many more good to know things for finding your job in Germany. 02.12. Assessment center: The supreme discipline among selection procedures Anmeldung Read more 02.12.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 - IBZ Munich - max. 20 participants - Language: German - Trainer: Eric Fritzsche In this seminar we prepare you for assessment centers in a practical way. 09.12. Rights and obligations at work in Germany: employment contract, salaries, references Anmeldung Read more 09.12.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 - Hansa Haus Munich (Läugerzimmer)- max. 20 participants - Language: English - Trainer: Heike Anne Dietzel - Career Coach Receiving a work contract is an exciting moment as it represents the last step to becoming a part of a company. Signing the contract will be legally binding and the contracts contains the most critical elements of your employeeship. Mandatory elements of a work contract under German labor law Types of employment and work contracts Most important rights and obligations of the employee and the employer Working hours and vacation regulations Probation period, termination of the contract and period of notice Final checklist before you sign the contract How your salary is calculated and what is composed of Work certificates & references in Germany and how to understand the secret code 16.12. LinkedIn workshop \"How To Use LinkedIn\" Anmeldung Read more [abgesagt] 16.12.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 Uhr - Hansa Haus München (Läugerzimmer) - max 20 TN - Sprache: Deutsch - Trainerin: Susanne Kößler Der Workshop richtet sich an alle Studierenden, die durch gezieltes und praxisnahes Training ein erfolgreiches berufliches Netzwerk über LinkedIn auf- oder ausbauen wollen. Anhand wertvoller Praxisbeispiele tauchen wir in die Welt des Netzwerkes ein. Sie erhalten praktische Hilfestellungen, wie Sie Ihr Profil am besten nutzen können und welche Möglichkeiten Sie damit haben. up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close Schließen"
