back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Q4 Internship Flash Meet & Greet LMU Karriereforum Working here & abroad: your international career in Bavaria Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal advice Career mentoring Offers for International Students Ambassador Program Internships abroad Cultural & sporting events Our services for employers Privacy policy career events & services User-Support for our portal Application tips for students Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene News and events Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Menu open Menu close You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services Career and networking events Workshops and Seminars You are here: Microsoft Certificate AI & IT-Security AI&I Are you interested in artificial intelligence and want to understand how AI can influence your studies and professional life? In our practice-oriented seminar you will learn what AI agents really are, how to develop them, and how to use them effectively. For students of all faculties! AI & I Dates 2026 Registration Read more February 6, 2026 - AI Case Workshop with EY Parthenon : Registration April 20, 2026 - AI Case Workshop with Ecodynamics - Opportunities and Impacts of AI Agents on Companies and Business Models (online) Registration May 15, 2026 - AI Case Workshop with Viola Kraus - Making Everyday Office Life More Efficient with AI (online) Registration June 5, 2026 - AI Case Workshop with the LMU AI HUB - Niklas Ippisch: With a Little Help from a Friend: Utilizing LLMs in Programming in R Registration June 19, 2026 - AI Case Workshop with Audi/LMU - Felix Ehlers - CANCELED: Rescheduled for December 4, 2026! June 26, 2026 - AI Case Workshop with GEMA / Maximilian Balluff, Head of AI Engineering: Data, Music, and AI: Building Robust Solutions Beyond the Prototype Registration July 3, 2026 AI Case Workshop with Ecodynamics : Fundamentals and Working with OpenClaw (online) Registration July 10, 2026 - AI Case Workshop @Career Talk with LRZ Munich : Registration July 17, 2026 - AI Case Workshop with Ecodynamics Masterclass 1 (online) Registration September 25, 2026 - AI Case Workshop with JetBrains - AI & Code with PyCharm & Co Registration October 16, 2026 - AI Case Workshop with Microsoft : Empowered by AI - Career and Skill Development. Xheneta Krasniqi Registration October 23, 2026 - AI IT / AI Case Workshop with EY Parthenon : Registration October 30, 2026 - AI Case Workshop with Ecodynamics Masterclass 2 (online) Registration November 6, 2026 - AI Case Workshop with the Artificial Intelligence Center Hamburg (ARIC) - Maria Tcharnetsky: AI & Ethics: What Should We Look Out For, and Do We Need a New Ethical Compass? Registration 11/20/26 - AI Case Workshop with GEMA Registration Nov. 27, 2026 AI Case Workshop with LMU - Dr. Stephan Pflaum: From the Perfect Prompt to a Personal Agent. (online) Registration 12/04/26 - AI Case Workshop with AUDI/LMU : Business vs. Academia Registration 12/11/26 AI Case Workshop with THINKaDo - Alexander Vocelka: AI Governance for a Prosperous Future - How to Co-Exist Registration Over the next few weeks, we will schedule the topics across the various dates. Each module will be available for individual registration. Artificial intelligence has long been a part of our everyday lives—but do you know how it works and how you can use it yourself? In this interactive seminar series, you’ll gain a practical, easy-to-understand, and well-founded introduction to the world of AI agents. Whether you plan to work in research, business, media, government, or NGOs in the future, a basic understanding of AI and its potential applications is becoming increasingly important. We are offering this seminar series in cooperation with: Microsoft Ecodynamics EY Parthenon GEMA LMU AI Hub Leibniz Computing Center SAP What to Expect: The AI Academy offers both beginners and advanced learners a wealth of practical content on the application of AI in various learning, teaching, work, and everyday environments. All seminars are designed to be hands-on. In addition to the opportunities, we also highlight the risks of this new technology, which has become indispensable. The overarching theme: how to use AI correctly and effectively in various fields. Target audience: Students from all disciplines in the humanities, social sciences, natural sciences, linguistics, and business—no prior knowledge required! Join us and learn how to use AI effectively in your studies and career. This project is also currently being turned into a book: The AI Compass for Students: How to Use AI Effectively in Your Studies and Career. (Expected to be published in 2026 by Springer Gabler) Personal AI Consultation on Monday Boost Your Workflow: The AI Consultation Mondays | 10:00 – 10:30 a.m. | Register via our portal Come by for an AI consultation . In 30 minutes, we'll explore how to get the most out of your prompts and agents. What we can talk about: Prompt Engineering: How to phrase prompts so that the AI delivers exactly what you asked for. AI Agents & Automation: From simple chat requests to assistants that handle complex workflows. Study Hacks: How to Use AI Effectively for Research, Coding, or Organizing Your Work. Tool Review: ChatGPT, Claude, Copilot, or Local LLMs – Which One Is Right for Your Project? You're also welcome to bring up any personal issues you may have during the consultation. Dr.phil. Stephan Pflaum LMU's Career Services Consultant Career Events & Services / Deputy Head of Career Service Send an email Zoom appointment for employers More Anfrage Workshop Formular Your company: * Your industry * Title of your AI case workshop * Brief description of the case in 2–3 sentences * Target student group * Economics Humanities Social Sciences STEM Law Degree level * Bachelor´s Master´s State Examination Doctorate Stage of studies Beginning Middle (internship phase) End (transition to the workforce) Contact person’s name * Email for inquiries * Data protection Information o data protection is available in LMU’s privacy policy. I consent to the processing of my data for the purpose of handling this contact request. * Submit 29:58 Cancel up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close Schließen"
