tems at the next level Gain experience abroad Overview: Gain experience abroad Internships abroad 6 Sub-items at the next level Internships abroad Overview: Internships abroad Finding an internship abroad 2 Sub-items at the next level Finding an internship abroad Overview: Finding an internship abroad Travel and safety information Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Scholarships 5 Sub-items at the next level Scholarships Overview: Scholarships Erasmus+ Traineeship Programme Career Service Scholarship PROMOS LMU Additional scholarships Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal stories Internships abroad Online Job Portals for International Internships Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Career Services 14 Sub-items at the next level Career Services Overview: Career Services Partner Companies Job portal 2 Sub-items at the next level Job portal Overview: Job portal Manual Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Career and networking events 10 Sub-items at the next level Career and networking events Overview: Career and networking events Career Talk Career Marathon Meet & Greet - Learn & Apply Career Trek Workshops and Seminars 8 Sub-items at the next level Workshops and Seminars Overview: Workshops and Seminars Seminars for acquiring soft skills and application-relevant knowledge Knowledge relevant to job applications and careers Subject-specific courses Microsoft Certificate AI & IT-Security Business administration and then finally weekend! Seminars for International Students Business language courses Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Q4 Internship Flash Meet & Greet LMU Karriereforum Working here & abroad: your international career in Bavaria Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal advice Career mentoring Offers for International Students Ambassador Program Internships abroad Cultural & sporting events Our services for employers Privacy policy career events & services User-Support for our portal Application tips for students Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene News and events Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Menu open Menu close You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services Career and networking events Workshops and Seminars You are here: Seminars for International Students Seminars for International Students Dates for wintersemester 2024/25 Skip to content 09.09. Future of Work - AI and Career 23.09. How do I present myself at a job interview? 21.10. Strategic and effective Jobsearch 25.11. Application Workshop for International Students 09.12. Rights and obligations at work in Germany: employment contract, salaries, references Show more 09.09. Future of Work - AI and Career Anmeldung Read more 09.09.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 - online (Zoom) - max 20 participants - Language: English - Trainer: Viola Kraus \"Future of Work - How the topic of (generative) AI will challenge us now and in the future and how we can learn to deal with it in order to make use of it\" Everyone is talking about AI, generative AI (GenAI). Companies want to use it in a targeted manner and some of us are asking ourselves \"what do I need to know, what else should I learn\". As an active member of our society, as future employees and teachers, we can prepare ourselves for these complex questions and the unknown. What should we already know and what can we still learn? Which gadgets can be used where and how, and are they used by companies? What unknowns are we likely to have to deal with? And what contribution can each of us make to society? 23.09. How do I present myself at a job interview? Anmeldung Read more 23.09.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 - Hansa Haus München (Läugerzimmer) - max 20 participants - Language: English - Trainer: Eva Kraatz In this workshop you will get a good understanding of how to prepare for a job interview. The following topics will be covered: General preparation for your job interview: Company and market environment About me (skills, questions, expectations, how I fit in with the company, etc.) Basic information on interview situations and more 21.10. Strategic and effective Jobsearch Anmeldung Read more 21.10.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 - Hansa Haus Munich (Läugerzimmer) - max 20 participants - Language: English - Trainer: Heike Anne Dietzel - Career Coach Searching for a new job can be a very time-consuming and long effort: there are hundreds of job search engines, matching portals and Companies post their vacancies on social media. What is the most effective way to find a new job? Get a glimpse behind the scenes of the recruiting process Build your application strategy that matches your background, personality and interests Understand the variety and evaluate job search channels for your needs Do's and Dont's for your communication with Hiring Managers and Recruiters during your job search Define effective networking channels for job search 25.11. Application Workshop for International Students Anmeldung Read more 25.11.2024 - 10:00 - 16:00 - live&local - Hansa Haus Munich (hall) - max. 20 participants - language: English - Trainer: Janine Müller Other countries, other manners - applying for your first job in Germany Getting started for your first job in Germany can be irritating. We will give you a good overview about the way to apply for a job in Germany among the candidate lifecycle: How to read job advertisements? What to prepare for the formal application? How can you prepare yourself for the job interview to make a great first impression? What is necessary to know for you first day and the onboarding period? ...and many more good to know things for finding your job in Germany. 09.12. Rights and obligations at work in Germany: employment contract, salaries, references Anmeldung Read more 09.12.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 - Hansa Haus Munich (Läugerzimmer)- max. 20 participants - Language: English - Trainer: Heike Anne Dietzel - Career Coach Receiving a work contract is an exciting moment as it represents the last step to becoming a part of a company. Signing the contract will be legally binding and the contracts contains the most critical elements of your employeeship. Mandatory elements of a work contract under German labor law Types of employment and work contracts Most important rights and obligations of the employee and the employer Working hours and vacation regulations Probation period, termination of the contract and period of notice Final checklist before you sign the contract How your salary is calculated and what is composed of Work certificates & references in Germany and how to understand the secret code up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close Schließen"
    },
