xperience abroad 2 Sub-items at the next level Gain experience abroad Overview: Gain experience abroad Internships abroad 6 Sub-items at the next level Internships abroad Overview: Internships abroad Finding an internship abroad 2 Sub-items at the next level Finding an internship abroad Overview: Finding an internship abroad Travel and safety information Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Scholarships 5 Sub-items at the next level Scholarships Overview: Scholarships Erasmus+ Traineeship Programme Career Service Scholarship PROMOS LMU Additional scholarships Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal stories Internships abroad Online Job Portals for International Internships Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Career Services 14 Sub-items at the next level Career Services Overview: Career Services Partner Companies Job portal 2 Sub-items at the next level Job portal Overview: Job portal Manual Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Career and networking events 10 Sub-items at the next level Career and networking events Overview: Career and networking events Career Talk Career Marathon Meet & Greet - Learn & Apply Career Trek Workshops and Seminars 8 Sub-items at the next level Workshops and Seminars Overview: Workshops and Seminars Seminars for acquiring soft skills and application-relevant knowledge Knowledge relevant to job applications and careers Subject-specific courses Microsoft Certificate AI & IT-Security Business administration and then finally weekend! Seminars for International Students Business language courses Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Q4 Internship Flash Meet & Greet LMU Karriereforum Working here & abroad: your international career in Bavaria Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal advice Career mentoring Offers for International Students Ambassador Program Internships abroad Cultural & sporting events Our services for employers Privacy policy career events & services User-Support for our portal Application tips for students Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene News and events Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Menu open Menu close You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services Career and networking events You are here: Working here & abroad: your international career in Bavaria LMU International Career Event \"Working here & abroad\" 2026 This event is aimed at international students at LMU and all students who are interested in working in an international environment. Date: November 13, 2026 Registration for workshops recommended. Participation in the career fair (from 12:00 noon) is also possible spontaneously and without pre-registration. Working in an international environment Enlarge Twice a year, we offer this event, which is aimed not only at domestic students but especially at international students. Date for the winter semester: November 13, 2026 Are you a student with an international background looking to establish a long-term career in the German job market? Building personal connections with local companies is a particularly important step in this process! Our event gives you the opportunity to do just that. You’ll meet companies with a presence both in Germany and internationally and discuss your career prospects and entry-level opportunities with them. Representatives from the Bavarian University Centers will also be on hand to offer guidance. Are you a student interested in working in an international environment and looking for the right starting point? This event offers you great opportunities to establish lasting personal connections with international employers from the business, social, and political sectors. The Bavarian University Centers in attendance will provide career counseling (including in academia) within their respective country groups. We recommend that you have German language skills at the B2 level. Sign up! for the event Read more The fair will be accompanied by workshops on professional networking, job applications, and starting a career. This year, for the first time, there will be an afternoon panel discussion featuring international LMU alumni who have successfully entered the German job market . Under the theme “My Career Journey in Germany,” three international alumni will share their paths to their careers, as well as their experiences, challenges, obstacles, and lessons learned. Afterward, you’ll have the opportunity to ask questions. The discussion will be held in English. Registration is recommended. Zhixin Liu , Consultant in the Technology & Transformation practice @Deloitte Pengyang Gao , Treasury Specialist, Shared Services @Toyota Kreditbank / Toyota Financial Services Germany Ke Zhang , Investment Risk Analyst at Allianz Commercial Venue: Kardinal Wendel Haus, Munich Participating Companies & Organizations Amazon amiga München BAMF (Hotline „Arbeiten und Leben in Deutschland“) BAYHOST - Bayerisches Hochschulzentrum für Mittel-, Ost- und Südosteuropa BTHA - Bayerisch-Tschechische Hochschulagentur BayFrance - Bayerisch-Französisches Hochschulzentrum Goethe Institut innoscripta LMU International Internships Make it in Germany: das Portal der Bundesregierung für Fachkräfte aus dem Ausland Mediaschool Bayern MUNTUM - Model United Nations (MUN) SwissRe TEG The Entrepreneurial Group ThirdBridge UNICEF UniCredit This list is updated regularly. Schedule Hop-on-hop-off concept: You decide when to join and leave the event. 9:00 a.m. - 10:30 a.m. Workshop I : \"Design Your International Career through Design Thinking\" (Violaine Storp) - Registration 10:30 a.m. - 12:00 p.m. Workshop II : \"Job Applications on the International Job Market\" (Viola Kraus) - Registration 11:30 a.m. - 1:30 p.m. Networking Lunch for Students, Companies, and Organizations 12:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Career Fair , Networking 3:00 p.m. - 4:30 p.m. \"My Career Journey in Germany!\" - Success Stories & Panel Discussion - Registration International LMU alumni share their stories of successful careers in Germany. Impressions 2024 & 2025 1 of 15 Previous Next Dieses Projekt wird aus Mitteln des Bayerischen Staatsministeriums für Familie, Arbeit und Soziales gefördert. Funding partners Johanna Uitz, M.A. LMU's Career Services Consultant for Internationalization & Employability / project manager FIT-LMU International Careers, Events & Seminars, Mentoring, Employer Services Send an email More up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close Schließen"
