el Gain experience abroad Overview: Gain experience abroad Internships abroad 6 Sub-items at the next level Internships abroad Overview: Internships abroad Finding an internship abroad 2 Sub-items at the next level Finding an internship abroad Overview: Finding an internship abroad Travel and safety information Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Scholarships 5 Sub-items at the next level Scholarships Overview: Scholarships Erasmus+ Traineeship Programme Career Service Scholarship PROMOS LMU Additional scholarships Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal stories Internships abroad Online Job Portals for International Internships Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Career Services 14 Sub-items at the next level Career Services Overview: Career Services Partner Companies Job portal 2 Sub-items at the next level Job portal Overview: Job portal Manual Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Career and networking events 10 Sub-items at the next level Career and networking events Overview: Career and networking events Career Talk Career Marathon Meet & Greet - Learn & Apply Career Trek Workshops and Seminars 8 Sub-items at the next level Workshops and Seminars Overview: Workshops and Seminars Seminars for acquiring soft skills and application-relevant knowledge Knowledge relevant to job applications and careers Subject-specific courses Microsoft Certificate AI & IT-Security Business administration and then finally weekend! Seminars for International Students Business language courses Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Q4 Internship Flash Meet & Greet LMU Karriereforum Working here & abroad: your international career in Bavaria Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal advice Career mentoring Offers for International Students Ambassador Program Internships abroad Cultural & sporting events Our services for employers Privacy policy career events & services User-Support for our portal Application tips for students Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene News and events Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Menu open Menu close You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services You are here: Personal advice Personal advice on careers and career entry We advise LMU students and doctoral candidates on all aspects of careers and career entry. Our advisory services for LMU students and doctoral candidates Career coaching for students and doctoral candidates Sign up If you are enrolled at LMU Munich, you can take advantage of personal and individualized advice offered through our Career Services. Expect a consultation to last about one hour. Possible topics to explore might be: Your career goals Your future prospects post bachelor, master or doctorate degree Your career entry Your job application questions Your employment opportunities For a personal consultation, please register in our portal. Under event participation you will find, among other services, personal career counseling. The interviews take place either online or on-site. Please get in touch with us as early as possible, as we always have a lot of requests and waiting times may sometimes be a little longer than expected. Application coaching for students and doctoral candidates Sign up Get your questions concerning your application answered in an individual Zoom session or a local appointment. Possible topics: Application process Job intervies Application documents (e.g. feedback on application letters) Assessment center CV-Check / Job reference-Check Sign up CV-Check Sign up Job reference-Check We will give you feedback on your CV or job reference. Procedure: Sign up via the LMU Career portal . Upload all relevant documents. Please arrange an appointment with us via our online calendar. We will then contact you... via video conference (Zoom or Skype): Job reference-Check or via email: CV-Check You can also find tips and advice on your application documents here . We ask you to implement the tips before booking a CV-Check. Advice on internships abroad We are currently not offering in-person counseling for internships abroad. If you have any questions, please contact us at praktika.careerservice@lmu.de You can find more information about internships abroad here . Career coaching for LMU alumni Did you study at LMU and have now been working for several years? Have you gained important experience during your professional career, achieved goals, and learned from your mistakes? We offer our graduates individual sessions based on the concepts and methodologies of systemic coaching. In a one-to-one session, we will help you to identify your individual goals, plan next steps, overcome potential barriers and move forward in your personal and professional development. These sessions take place in a safe environment. Confidentiality is guaranteed. Possible topics you may bring to the table include: Decision making Professional (re)orientation Evaluation of personal competences and resources Dealing with current challenges Establishing future prospects in terms of your personal or professional development Target group LMU Munich graduates with a maximum of ten years professional experience gained after graduation. Next steps Please write your coaching topic in a short email to us and we will contact you for an appointment. Pricing / Organization One coaching hour (approx. 60 minutes) costs 120,- Euro. The first hour serves to get to know each other and to answer any unanswered questions about the coaching process and is therefore free of charge. Depending on the topic, a structured coaching process can last up to five hours. The duration of the coaching process and the individual appointments are coordinated between coach and coachee. The meetings take place in a central, quiet location in Munich or via video conference. What coaching is certainly not Coaching is neither a form of training nor a formal professional attainment. Specific proposals for actions to be taken or solutions to problems are not offered by the coach and no typical \"advice\" is given. Coaching is not a substitute for psychological, psychotherapeutic or psychiatric advice or treatment. Please note that we do not coach LMU employees in view of possible conflicting interests. Career counseling for LMU junior academics As you embark on your academic career path, different questions will arise. Let us support you with services to help you define and achieve your career goals.Support for doctoral candidates. Counseling academic careers Support for doctoral candidates Please understand that in certain cases we may not be able to offer our counseling services at all, or only to a limited extent. This applies in particular to potential conflicts of interest , as well as when the nature of a counseling request overlaps with legal counseling, therapeutic counseling, or other protected forms of counseling . If you have previously been employed, are currently employed, or are seeking employment at LMU - for example, as a student or research assistant, as a faculty member, or as a researcher - we therefore reserve the right to refer you to an appropriate external counseling service . This is to ensure independent, professionally appropriate counseling and to protect all parties involved. up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close Schließen"
    },
