vel Gain experience abroad Overview: Gain experience abroad Internships abroad 6 Sub-items at the next level Internships abroad Overview: Internships abroad Finding an internship abroad 2 Sub-items at the next level Finding an internship abroad Overview: Finding an internship abroad Travel and safety information Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Scholarships 5 Sub-items at the next level Scholarships Overview: Scholarships Erasmus+ Traineeship Programme Career Service Scholarship PROMOS LMU Additional scholarships Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal stories Internships abroad Online Job Portals for International Internships Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Career Services 14 Sub-items at the next level Career Services Overview: Career Services Partner Companies Job portal 2 Sub-items at the next level Job portal Overview: Job portal Manual Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Career and networking events 10 Sub-items at the next level Career and networking events Overview: Career and networking events Career Talk Career Marathon Meet & Greet - Learn & Apply Career Trek Workshops and Seminars 8 Sub-items at the next level Workshops and Seminars Overview: Workshops and Seminars Seminars for acquiring soft skills and application-relevant knowledge Knowledge relevant to job applications and careers Subject-specific courses Microsoft Certificate AI & IT-Security Business administration and then finally weekend! Seminars for International Students Business language courses Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Q4 Internship Flash Meet & Greet LMU Karriereforum Working here & abroad: your international career in Bavaria Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal advice Career mentoring Offers for International Students Ambassador Program Internships abroad Cultural & sporting events Our services for employers Privacy policy career events & services User-Support for our portal Application tips for students Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene News and events Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Menu open Menu close You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services You are here: Career mentoring LMU Career Mentoring program - Your tandem to success Is my dream job just a dream? Will I manage the transition from studying to working? How can I stand out in my job application? Which core qualifications should I have? How do I make career contacts? These are lots of questions. Have you thought about reaching out to someone who is already in the job, industry or company that you'd like to be? Skip to content Greeting from Minister of State Ulrike Scharf (StMAS) The LMU Career Mentoring Programme at a glance Further information on the procedure and registration Insights LMU Career Mentoring Forum 2026 Introducing a mentoring tandem Dieses Projekt wird aus Mitteln des Bayerischen Staatsministeriums für Familie, Arbeit und Soziales gefördert. Show more Greeting from Minister of State Ulrike Scharf (StMAS) If you click to view this video your personal data will be transmitted to YouTube and cookies may also be stored on your device. LMU has no influence over how any such data is transmitted or indeed over its further usage. More information available here: LMU data protection policy , data protection policy from YouTube / Google I acknowledge that I have read and understood the information concerning the protection of my data and am willing to display the embedded content despite potential risks. 2:00\n\t\t\t\t        \t\t | \n\t\t\t\t\t        \t22 Nov 2024\n\t\t\t\t        \t\t |  \n\t\t\t\t        \t\t\t©StMAS The LMU Career Mentoring Programme at a glance Registration for mentees & mentors Read more Your mentoring relationship is one of the best opportunities to reflect on your professional and personal plans with an experienced person . Often, your mentor will be your direct guide to your first job. Our approximately 300 volunteer mentors are experienced academics from all disciplines and from a wide variety of industries and professions . They answer your questions, share their experiences and accompany you to help you get your career off to a successful start. Our mentees and mentors agree: mentoring is great fun and helps them advance both professionally and personally. The fact that many former mentees return to us as mentors a few years later speaks for itself. The duration of the mentoring tandems is entirely individual: anything is possible, from a few weeks to several months or even long-term relationships, depending on the needs of the mentees and the capacities of the mentors. How often you meet is also individual: as a rule, mentors and mentees meet in person once or twice every six months and also keep in touch by telephone or email. In the tandem, you can freely discuss all topics related to starting your career, your studies and your career . Topics, times and locations are determined by the mentor and mentee themselves. During various events , such as the golf event or theatre visits, both sides can expand their network to include other mentors and students. Further information on the procedure and registration Information & registration for students Sign up If you are enrolled at LMU – whether as an undergraduate or doctoral student – you can register as a mentee at any time. Your field of study or semester of study are irrelevant. After you register, we will support you in selecting your mentor in a personal consultation. LMU Career Mentoring process: Register as a student at any time via the Career Service Portal . Fill out your personal profile completely. Register for the Career Mentoring Programme via the portal (important: include a brief description of your motivation). Select a date for the ‘mentoring interview’ (Zoom or on-site). After the interview, we will provide you with a selection of suitable mentors. Please select up to two mentors. As soon as the person you have chosen has agreed to the tandem, you will receive a confirmation email from us. Get in touch with your mentor! You and your mentor will design your tandem individually. You will decide together how often you meet, whether in person or virtually, whether you keep in touch beyond that, and what you talk about. Information & registration for mentors Sign up Are you an academic with three or more years of professional experience ? Then we would be delighted to have you join our programme as a volunteer mentor. We welcome LMU alumni and graduates from other universities who have the time and desire to volunteer as mentors to support LMU students in their career choices. We welcome mentors from all industries and professional fields. We offer virtual exchange and networking meetings for our mentors several times a year. In addition, we organise cultural or sporting exchange meetings in and around LMU at regular intervals. Mentors also receive a free copy of our Mentoring Compass book. LMU Career Mentoring procedure: Please register once on the LMU Career Service Portal . Fill out your personal profile in full. Then register for the Career Mentoring Programme via ‘Events & Services’. It is important to provide information about your professional background and your motivation, as this information will be displayed to the students. If you are interested, please register directly for a virtual introductory webinar or further exchange meetings. Late registration is possible at any time. As soon as a student has chosen you as their mentor, we will notify you. You then have the option of accepting or rejecting the pairing via the portal. Once you have agreed, your mentee will contact you shortly. Please be patient – it can sometimes take a few weeks for the first match to be made. We hold weekly selection interviews with students from all departments. If you have any questions, please feel free to contact us at any time by email . You and your mentee will design your tandem individually. You will decide together how often you meet, whether in person or virtually, whether you keep in touch beyond that, and what you talk about. Events for mentors LMU Mentoring-Forum: annual networking and exchange event with keynote speeches on the topic of mentoring (6–9 p.m., Literaturhaus Munich) Thursday, march 5 2026 Sign up! Introductory webinars for new mentors (18:30 - 19:30, Zoom) Tuesday, May 19, 2026 Sign up! Tuesday, September 22, 2026 Sign up! Tuesday, December 8, 2026 Sign up! Mentoring consultation hours for mentors – questions, exchange, networking (18:30 - 19:30, Zoom) Tuesday, April 14, 2026 Sign up! Tuesday, October 6, 2026 Sign up! Voraussetzung: Vollständige Registrierung als Mentor / Mentorin Insights LMU Career Mentoring Forum 2026 The LMU Career Mentoring Forum 2026 took place on March 5 at the Literaturhaus München. The program included personal exchanges, networking, and substantive input on the topic of mentoring. 1 of 8 Previous Next Introducing a mentoring tandem If you click to view this video your personal data will be transmitted to YouTube and cookies may also be stored on your device. LMU has no influence over how any such data is transmitted or indeed over its further usage. More information available here: LMU data protection policy , data protection policy from YouTube / Google I acknowledge that I have read and understood the information concerning the protection of my data and am willing to display the embedded content despite potential risks. 19 Jan 2021 Dieses Projekt wird aus Mitteln des Bayerischen Staatsministeriums für Familie, Arbeit und Soziales gefördert. Johanna Uitz, M.A. LMU's Career Services Consultant for Internationalization & Employability / project manager FIT-LMU International Careers, Events & Seminars, Mentoring, Employer Services Send an email More Dr.phil. Stephan Pflaum LMU's Career Services Consultant Career Events & Services / Deputy Head of Career Service Send an email Zoom appointment for employers More up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close Schließen"
