zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Q4 Internship Flash Meet & Greet LMU Karriereforum Working here & abroad: your international career in Bavaria Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal advice Career mentoring Offers for International Students Ambassador Program Internships abroad Cultural & sporting events Our services for employers Privacy policy career events & services User-Support for our portal Application tips for students Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene News and events Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Menu open Menu close You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services You are here: Offers for International Students Career Services for International Students & Doctoral Candidates We support international students & doctoral candidates at LMU with customized services to help them gain a foothold in the German job market. Skip to content Career events and seminars 2026 September 2026 October 2026 November 2026 Business German courses Personal counseling services LMU Career Mentoring Program Additional Sources of Information Your contact Dieses Projekt wird aus Mitteln des Bayerischen Staatsministeriums für Familie, Arbeit und Soziales gefördert. Funding partners Show more Enlarge Are you a student with an international background and want to gain a foothold in the Bavarian or German job market? Whether you are interested in internships, working student positions, part-time jobs or a permanent position in a German-speaking country - we will support you on your career path. We offer international students of the LMU exclusive Career events, Seminars Professional language courses and Personal consulting services On this website you will find an overview of our services. Career events and seminars 2026 You are of course cordially invited to all career events. You can find an overview of all events here . September 2026 07.09.2026 Successful use of Artificial Intelligence in the Job Application Process (online, EN) 07.09.2026 | 2 - 6 pm | Zoom | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Viola Kraus Sign up! Artificial Intelligence is rapidly transforming how we search for jobs, prepare applications, and present ourselves to employers. At the same time, organizations are increasingly using AI-stools in recruiting and selection. But what does this mean for you, entering the job market? In this interactive 4-hour online workshop, you will gain a practical overview of the role of AI in today's job application process and learn about current developments. Together, we will explore how to use AI effectively and responsibly when preparing applications, CVs, cover letters, and interview preparations. The workshop combines expert input with hands-on exercises, reflection, and peer exchange. You will actively work on examples, discuss trends, and get time to individually work on your AI driven recruiting strategy and documents. By the end of the workshop, you will: Understand how AI is changing recruitment and hiring practices. Learn how AI can support different stages of your application process. Gain practical tips and develop ideas for preparing your future career in a changing world of work. 14.09.2026 LinkedIn for Career Starters: How to land a job with the right profile? (online, EN) 14.09.2026 | 2 - 4 pm | Zoom | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Julia Barden Sign up! Would you like to create a convincing LinkedIn profile that leaves a positive impression on potential employers? Are you unsure how to present your qualifications convincingly? Would you like to actively use your LinkedIn profile for your job search? The workshop is highly practical. After every short theory input, you will have time to work directly on your own LinkedIn profile while receiving examples, guidance and practical tips. By the end of the workshop, you will have a professional, (almost) complete LinkedIn profile that is ready to support your job search, as well as a clear understanding of how to use it effectively. In this online workshop you will learn: How to create a professional LinkedIn profile from scratch What to write in each important profile section, including your headline, About section, experience, education and skills How recruiters search for candidates and how to optimize your profile to appear in search results How to use keywords strategically How to use LinkedIn effectively for job searching and networking 21.09.2026 Strategic and effective Jobsearch (online, EN) 21.09.2026 | 2 - 6 pm | online (Zoom) | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Carolin Martin Sign up! Gain fundermantal insights into the hiring process (AI aspects included) while learning how to build a compelling personal brand and defining your ideal career profile. Develop your application strategy, prepare your documents accordingly and discover practical interview techniques to help you stand out with confidence. Having lead the Recruting team at Apple Retail in Germany for more than 10 years our trainer will share all her knowledge, actionalbe tools and a clear plan for your successful jobsearch. 28.09.2026 Salary negotiations: How to handle the tricky question with confidence (online, EN) 28.09.2026 | 4 - 6 pm | Zoom | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Janine Müller Sign up! Salary discussions can be challenging - but with the right preparation, they become an opportunity. In this two-hour online seminar, participants explore salary and benefits models, understand what influences pay, prepare for interviews and compensation talks, and gain valuable insights into the EU Pay Transparency Directive. October 2026 12.10.2026 Legal framework for working in Germany: Rights and obligations, employment contract, salaries, references (online, EN) 12.10.2026 | 2 - 5 pm | online (Zoom) | 20 participants max | Language: englis h | Trainer: Violaine Storp Sign up! Seminar Topics: Mandatory elements of a work contract under German labour law Types of employment and work contracts Most important rights and obligations of the employee and the employer Working hours and vacation regulations Probation period, termination of the contract and period of notice Final checklist before you sign the contract How your salarly is calculated and what is is composed of Work certificates & references in Germany and how to understand the secret code 26.10.2026 Young Leadership Skills – First Steps into Leadership/ Supervision (on site, EN) 26.10.2026 | 2 - 6 pm | Hansa Haus München | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Viola Kraus Sign up! Leadership or supervision skills are essential in many careers, in different stages of your life. Whether you are planning a career in business, science, public service, or academia, the ability to lead yourself and others is a critical skill. This interactive 4-hour online workshop offers a practical introduction to the foundations of effective leadership/supervision. Together, we will explore key topics that young professionals encounter when taking responsibility for projects, teams, or initiatives: Core responsibilities and expectations of a leadership role + common leadership styles The fundamentals of communication How to navigate difficult conversations Giving and receiving constructive feedback Understanding your own expectations, values, and leadership mindset Through practical examples, reflection exercises, and interactive discussions, you will gain valuable insights into what successful leadership looks like and how you can begin developing your own leadership style. We suggest to take the www.16personalities.com prior to our workshop to gain some initial insights and then come and join our interactive session. November 2026 02.11.2026 Making career & professional decisions (on site, EN) 02.11.2026 | 2 - 6 pm | Hansa Haus München | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Eva Kraatz Sign up! What will I do after college? Which job and which professional environment are the best fit for me? What exactly do I want? There are so many possibilities—which one is right for me? Deciding which career path to pursue after graduation isn’t always easy. In this seminar, we’ll explore our personal values, among other things, because they play a crucial role in shaping our lives—even if we’re often unaware of it. When we understand our values, we can make career decisions that are not only a good fit but also sustainable. The afternoon will be rounded out with various tips and tricks for general decision-making. In this workshop, we’ll cover the following topics: Hierarchy of personal values Tips and tricks for decision-making and more 16.11.2026 Application Workshop for Internationals (on site, EN) 16.11.2026 | 10 am - 4 pm | Hansa Haus München | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Janine Müller Sign up! Other countries, other manners - applying for your first job in Germany Getting started for your first job in Germany can be difficult. We will give you a good overview about the way to apply for a job in Germany among the candidate lifecycle: How to read job advertisements? What to prepare for the formal application? How can you prepare yourself for the job interview to make a great first impression? What is necessary to know for you first day and the onboarding period? ...and many more important things for finding your job in Germany. 30.11.2026 Navigating Germany: Building Intercultural Competences to Connect, Collaborate, and Thrive (online, EN) 30.11.2026 | 4 - 6 pm | Zoom | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Angela Kraft-Chan Sign up! Living and studying in Germany involves navigating more than just academic life. It means understanding unwritten rules: how feedback is handled, how trust is built with others, or how group dynamics work in projects, all of which feel different than back home. Thriving in an international career takes more than expertise, but also interpersonal skills to act across cultures. In this interactive workshop, you’ll learn to decode intercultural dynamics and develop practical skills to connect, communicate, and collaborate with greater confidence. Together, we'll explore: Key cultural dimensions such as communication, trust-building, or risk management styles, and how they show up in situations you already recognise How cultural differences can lead to misunderstandings, and what you can do about it Practical communication tools and phrases you can use right away You'll leave with: A clearer framework for understanding cultural differences Develop your own authentic communication style with hands on tools navigating intercultural moments More confidence to express and show up as your authentic self Who is this for? Internationals who want to feel more at ease and more effective in German social and professional settings; and locals who want to thrive in an increasingly intercultural environment. 13.11.2026 LMU International Career Event \"Working here & abroad\" Career & Networking event for international students & doctoral candidates from all faculties. 9:00 - 10:30 a.m. Workshop I : \"Design Your International Career through Design Thinking\" - Sign up! 10:30 a.m. - 12:00 p.m. Workshop II : \"Job Applications on the International Job Market\" - Sign up! 12:00 p.m. - 5:00 p.m Career Fair with up to 20 companies and organizations , Networking - Sing up! 3:00 - 4:30 p.m. \"My Career Journey in Germany!\" - International LMU alumni share their stories of successful careers in Germany. (panel discussion) - Sign up! More information can be found here . Business German courses Online Self-Study Course: “Starting a Career and Working Life in Germany” Online self-study course from Deutsch-Uni Online (DUO) Duration: approx. 100 hours Course level: B1; suitable for students at levels A2–B2 Free for students at LMU Munich. Registration . Tutored Professional Language Course “German for Career Starters” (B2/C1) Dates: New dates will be announced here In cooperation with Deutsch-Uni Online (DUO) This is an online course. The content is partly offered in a flexible self-study format , and you will also receive support from a tutor : 8 virtual group meetings (thursdays from 6:30 pm, 70 minutes each) 3 individual feedback sessions on submitted work 4 moderated topics in the forum Certificate of completion upon active participation Required language proficiency: B2 Time commitment: approx. 50 total learning hours Deposit: €75 (we will refund the deposit after the course ends if you have successfully completed at least 75% of the course) Topics: Well-prepared for the job interview Successful communication with colleagues Handling large amounts of information Project work Grammar topics: Causal structures, adjective declension, relative clauses, participial attributes, nominal and verbal style Please note that only students and doctoral candidates enrolled at LMU are eligible to take the course. Please upload your enrollment certificate via the portal. Personal counseling services Infos & Anmeldung Read more Take advantage of our wide range of personalized consulting services: Resume Check: The formal and content requirements vary depending on the country where you're applying. Let us review your resume or cover letter and receive valuable tips and advice via email. Job Reference Review: Have you received a job reference in a German-speaking country and would like feedback on it? Get that feedback during a brief, one-on-one conversation. Personal Career Counseling: Do you have questions about your prospects after graduation, your opportunities, or how to start your career? Get personalized, one-on-one advice on any questions you have about starting your career. Job Application Counseling: Do you have specific questions about your current job application? Ask us during a one-on-one consultation. You can find important information about German-language application materials here. Walk-in office hours* on Thursdays from 11 a.m. to 12 p.m. Address: Ludwigstraße 27, Room G211 No appointment necessary. We will notify you here if an office hour is canceled. *The open office hours are not a substitute for individual career or job application counseling and are intended solely as a first point of contact for general questions. Please note that time is limited. LMU Career Mentoring Program Enlarge Your mentoring relationship is one of the best opportunities to reflect on your professional and personal goals with an experienced person. Mentors often serve as direct guides to your first job. Our approximately 300 volunteer mentors are experienced professionals with college degrees in a wide range of fields, representing a diverse array of industries and occupations. The LMU Career Mentoring Program offers you the following benefits: You'll be assigned a personal contact - an experienced professional - who will be there to assist you with your questions and concerns. This will give you direct insights into your target industry, application processes, and the German job market. You'll have the opportunity to participate in a wide variety of events, allowing you to expand your personal and professional network in Germany. Information & Registration Additional Sources of Information We recommend that you achieve at least a B2 level of German proficiency before applying for jobs in German-speaking countries, as this is a requirement for many companies. Here you will find the general German courses offered at LMU. Volunteering can be a great way to meet people, practice German, and gain your first practical experience. You can find an overview of LMU student clubs and initiatives here . LMU International Student Guide LMU Gateway for International Doctoral Candidates Social Services and Scholarship Counseling for International Candidates Conflict Resolution and Anti-Discrimination Make it in Germany - the official website for qualified professionals The German government’s official multilingual portal , “Make it in Germany,” provides reliable information on all aspects of living and working in Germany. The website offers qualified professionals and international students all the relevant information on visas and residence permits, as well as on career prospects after completing their studies in Germany. Amiga Munich Your contact Johanna Uitz, M.A. LMU's Career Services Consultant for Internationalization & Employability / project manager FIT-LMU International Careers, Events & Seminars, Mentoring, Employer Services Send an email More Dieses Projekt wird aus Mitteln des Bayerischen Staatsministeriums für Familie, Arbeit und Soziales gefördert. Funding partners up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close Schließen"
