Navigationsebene Q4 Internship Flash Meet & Greet LMU Karriereforum Working here & abroad: your international career in Bavaria Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal advice Career mentoring Offers for International Students Ambassador Program Internships abroad Cultural & sporting events Our services for employers Privacy policy career events & services User-Support for our portal Application tips for students Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene News and events Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Menu open Menu close You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services You are here: Ambassador Program Peer-to-peer Ambassador Program Our new cohort of ambassadors will start in the winter semester 2024/25. The next introductory seminar will take place on 25.10.2024. To the application Become a student ambassador in the LMU Career Community! Link to registration Read more Our career network of students from all departments and companies, as well as mentors from all industries and professions, should continue to grow and enable you to successfully start your career. As one of 10 ambassadors per semester, you will help us inform students about our offerings and expand our reach. We will train you in an exclusive seminar to become a successful networker. You will receive a certificate from us about your commitment and training. Special attention is given to reaching our international students. So if you are an international student yourself, you are especially welcome to join our program! Your Ambassador Responsibilities: You support the LMU Career Community in growing. You make your fellow students aware of our community in lectures and seminars. In social networks such as Instagram or LinkedIn, you share our posts (with content suitable for you and your fellow students). You forward our information about events, seminars or consulting offers (that match your study / interest profile) to your friends. You will help us with the supervision of our trade fair stand. You help us establish a lasting connection with your faculty. You will be actively involved in our social media presence. If you are interested, you can also get involved in the implementation of our career events. Your advantages: In your first semester as an ambassador, we will train you to be a successful networker in an exclusive seminar . You will get insights \"behind the scenes\" of the Career Service and make a variety of contacts. You will always be up-to-date regarding our events and offers and will be partially involved in the planning. You will receive exclusive LMU Ambassador business cards. You will receive a certificate for your voluntary commitment as an ambassador. Your profile: You are at least in your second semester (Bachelor or Master). You are interested in career topics and active networking and share our information reliably and appropriately with your fellow students. You have already participated in some of our events. You are willing to actively support us as an ambassador for at least one semester. Ambassadors from all faculties of the LMU are welcome. To become an ambassador, please apply via our portal . Your contact More Dr.phil. Stephan Pflaum LMU's Career Services Consultant Career Events & Services / Deputy Head of Career Service Send an email Zoom appointment for employers More up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close Schließen"
