nternational Student Guide Overview: International Student Guide Checklists Health and safety Visa Registering your address Residence permit Opening a bank account Living costs Academic culture Working in Germany Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Student support services 8 Sub-items at the next level Student support services Overview: Student support services Finance your studies 2 Sub-items at the next level Finance your studies Overview: Finance your studies Scholarships 5 Sub-items at the next level Scholarships Overview: Scholarships Deutschlandstipendium 3 Sub-items at the next level Deutschlandstipendium Overview: Deutschlandstipendium Application Events Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Grants from foundation funds Oskar Karl Forster Scholarship Scholarships for international students Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Studying with a child 2 Sub-items at the next level Studying with a child Overview: Studying with a child International student parents Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Studying with a disability 6 Sub-items at the next level Studying with a disability Overview: Studying with a disability Advice and networking Special applications Compensation for disadvantages Barrier-free access and aids FAQs Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Studying in the first generation Workshops on study skills and co. IT service offers Peer support Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Gain experience abroad 2 Sub-items at the next level Gain experience abroad Overview: Gain experience abroad Internships abroad 6 Sub-items at the next level Internships abroad Overview: Internships abroad Finding an internship abroad 2 Sub-items at the next level Finding an internship abroad Overview: Finding an internship abroad Travel and safety information Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Scholarships 5 Sub-items at the next level Scholarships Overview: Scholarships Erasmus+ Traineeship Programme Career Service Scholarship PROMOS LMU Additional scholarships Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal stories Internships abroad Online Job Portals for International Internships Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Career Services 14 Sub-items at the next level Career Services Overview: Career Services Partner Companies Job portal 2 Sub-items at the next level Job portal Overview: Job portal Manual Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Career and networking events 10 Sub-items at the next level Career and networking events Overview: Career and networking events Career Talk Career Marathon Meet & Greet - Learn & Apply Career Trek Workshops and Seminars 8 Sub-items at the next level Workshops and Seminars Overview: Workshops and Seminars Seminars for acquiring soft skills and application-relevant knowledge Knowledge relevant to job applications and careers Subject-specific courses Microsoft Certificate AI & IT-Security Business administration and then finally weekend! Seminars for International Students Business language courses Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Q4 Internship Flash Meet & Greet LMU Karriereforum Working here & abroad: your international career in Bavaria Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Personal advice Career mentoring Offers for International Students Ambassador Program Internships abroad Cultural & sporting events Our services for employers Privacy policy career events & services User-Support for our portal Application tips for students Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene News and events Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Language version Deutsch Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion back zur vorherigen Navigationsebene Menu open Menu close You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services You are here: Our services for employers LMU career fairs & recruiting for employers As the central Career Services of LMU, we offer customized career events and services for more than 50,000 students from all faculties and companies from all sectors. Skip to content Talents Meet Companies Basic: Advertise on the LMU job portal Join the virtual LMU Career Fair! Premium services: Many do fairs. We design events! Overview of premium services Costs & Services LMU Career Event or classic fair? A comparison. Event dates for 2026 Event checklists FAQs for companies Guidelines of the LMU Career Services Your contact for all of LMU's Career Events & Fairs Show more Talents Meet Companies If you click to view this video your personal data will be transmitted to YouTube and cookies may also be stored on your device. LMU has no influence over how any such data is transmitted or indeed over its further usage. More information available here: LMU data protection policy , data protection policy from YouTube / Google I acknowledge that I have read and understood the information concerning the protection of my data and am willing to display the embedded content despite potential risks. This short film gives you exclusive insights into our career events. Find out directly from partner companies and students how they experience the events, what opportunities arise from them – and why it benefits you as an employer to be there. 5:12\n\t\t\t\t        \t\t | \n\t\t\t\t\t        \t10 Apr 2025\n\t\t\t\t        \t\t |  \n\t\t\t\t        \t\t\t©LMU Career Service Basic: Advertise on the LMU job portal Post your jobs here Read more You can publish your advertisements for part-time jobs, student traineeships, internships and permanent positions online on our job portal . This allows you to reach students from all subject areas and in all phases of their studies. We offer two options for the duration of publication, tailored to your recruiting needs. We guarantee you visibility and a high reach: The job portal is known to all students in Munich and is highly frequented (more than 1,000 visits/day). Quick guide job exchange In case of problems/questions: There is a support button in the portal. Here you can activate your account for seven days and we can help you quickly and directly. Internships Part-time jobs Working student positions Job advertisements Single advertisements for 4 weeks 90,- 180,- 180,- 240,- Long-term advertisements for 6 months 360,- 540,- 540,- 540,- All prices are listed in euros. Prices are net plus VAT. Please read our general terms & conditions - Discounts or contingent bookings are not possible. We reserve the right to charge a processing fee of 10 euros for any subsequent changes to the invoice details. As an alternative to bank transfer, you are welcome to use our ePayBayern system for payment. There you can pay by credit card, debit card, or PayPal. Please note that due to the high level of effort involved and in view of our modest invoice amounts, we only complete supplier forms for our premium partners. Many forms are designed for B2B contacts and companies that do not apply to us as a public corporation. You will find all the relevant information you need in the LMU Munich legal notice and on the website of the Free State of Bavaria . Team Job-Portal LMU's Career Services Office / Job portal Send an email More Join the virtual LMU Career Fair! Reach more than 50,000 of LMU’s top talents exclusively! Promote your career opportunities and events at two prominent locations. Virtual Career Fair Career & Networking Events 1 year for only EUR 2,995 (net). Secure your spot now and attract top talent for your events and your company. If you’re interested, please contact us. Premium services: Many do fairs. We design events! Book now Read more As LMU’s official Career Service , we have strong ties with all of LMU’s faculties. We are the only place where you can reach all of LMU’s more than 50,000 students in a way that precisely aligns with your defined recruiting goals. In addition to LMU students , students from other public universities and colleges are always welcome to attend our events. Students who take advantage of our events and services are among the most dedicated and successful at LMU. Our career network has grown steadily since 2012. Over 80 percent of the companies have been our clients for more than five years. They value the more intensive and lasting career connections fostered by our programs. In addition, the number of companies joining the network on the recommendation of our graduates increases every year. In 2024, 15 recommendations led to partnerships. We are committed to fostering sustainable and tailored career connections , always keeping the interests of both our students and our corporate partners equally in mind. Attendees at our career fairs consistently report that the interactions at our events are more meaningful and long-lasting , and more often lead to concrete hiring successes . Our events are always held in a pleasant atmosphere with appealing catering for both students and company representatives. Lasting professional connections within an excellent network Our career events and fairs are part of a premium partnership with LMU , as our goal is to foster lasting and tailored connections between students, graduates, and your company or organization. Join the extensive LMU career network and meet the students who match your recruitment profile. Overview of premium services Your advantages at a glance Please refer to the table below for the terms of the partnership. At our exclusive career events , you can get to know students personally and sustainably. We address the students according to your recruiting goals: Studienfach/fächer Phase des Studiums angestrebter Abschluss At all events, you will receive the CVs of the participants in advance so that you can conduct individual interviews with particularly interesting candidates on site and to keep in touch after the events. We also advertise your in-house events for you via our event calendar and in our monthly newsletter to all students. [ Registration form] You can post up to 10 job advertisements per semester free of charge on our job board . You have access to the LMU Talent Pool profiles. You can contact the candidates you are interested in directly at any time. For the duration of your membership, we offer you a virtual exhibition stand on our partner site and invite you to our cultural and sporting events with LMU alumni and students, e.g. the LMU Golf Community . Depending on the package booked, the partnership includes one or more free career treks to your company. As a partner, you can take part in new piloted trade fair formats free of charge . If you wish, you can organize business case workshops with a professionally selected group of students as part of the Q4 Internship Flash . Furthermore, our social media team will visit you on request to shoot an Insta story with you for your and our site. We also regularly report on our partner companies on LinkedIn . We also proactively connect you with students who match your advertised positions. Please book the events via our Career Community Portal . The contract is concluded after we have checked and confirmed the booking. Real Career Networking, Beyond Sharing Give Aways! At LMU Career Service events, you don't (just) impress our students with giveaways and a large exhibition stand. The focus is on your company, your representatives on site, your vision, your mission - in short, your employer brand. Our event participants - companies and students - often tell us afterwards that the career discussions at our events are more intensive, more concrete and more goal-oriented. The students are well prepared, inform themselves in advance about the participating companies and often approach recruiters and experts with concrete application plans . Our events are designed so that all companies have the same exhibition space available for tables, chairs, roll-ups and giveaways. We deliberately do not differentiate according to industry and company size . We provide tables, chairs, electricity, catering and co. Ideally, you come with two roll-ups, at least two representatives and, depending on the size of the event, giveaways for the students in attendance. Our advertising is impressive! With our regularly published flyers, posters and banners at the main building and at the main canteen, we advertise you and your events at LMU all year round at all LMU locations and at the \"Universität\" subway station. Costs & Services model Duration / Number of Career Events Total net price in EUR Premium #1 1 career event 1 Career Trek to your company Premium services for 6 months / 1 semester* 4,500 Premium #2 2 career events 1 free Career Trek Premium services for 12 months / 2 semesters* 25 job advertisements free of charge 6,000 Premium #3 Up to 4 career events 2 free Career Treks Premium services for 18 months / 3 semesters* 25 job advertisements free of charge 7,500 Booking Single Event 1 Career Event Participation with up to 3 company representatives 2,995 First and second extension of the partnership for existing customers Up to 4 career events 2 free Career Treks Free participation in the Q4 Internship Flash Premium services for 18 months / 3 semesters* 6,000 from the third consecutive renewal of the partnership Up to 4 career events 2 free Career Treks Free participation in the Q4 Internship Flash Premium services for 18 months / 3 semesters* 4,750 * In addition to participating in the event, you will have access to all other Career Service services mentioned above (e.g., talent pool, digital exhibition booth, promotion of your events, etc.) free of charge during the event period. LMU Career Event or classic fair? A comparison. What makes the LMU Career Service events so special? What advantages do they offer compared to regular career fairs? We have summarized the most important points for you. For comparison (PDF, 174 KB) As a partner company, please select your events here . Alternatively, feel free to contact us by email to make your event reservations. Event dates for 2026 Date Format March 27 LMU Shape Your Career! Consulting + STEM – our industry-specific career fair, attracting up to 300 students. Opportunity to host a keynote speech or workshop upon request. May 22 LMU Career Forum – our traditional career fair, attracting up to 300 students; option to host a keynote speech or workshop upon request July 10 LMU Career Talk – our career fair featuring a panel discussion in the morning and a fair in the afternoon, with up to 300 students in attendance ; opportunity to host a keynote speech or workshop upon request October 23 LMU Career Marathon – our fair focused on diversity and inclusion, offering up to 300 students the opportunity to attend a keynote speech or workshop upon request November 13 International Career Event \" Working Here & Abroad \" – our career fair for all students with an international background and/or international career plans. Opportunity to attend a keynote speech or workshop upon request Ongoing and by appointment Every Tuesday at the Literaturhaus or Kardinal Wendel Haus Meet & Greet – As a company, you’ll visit us and meet students who match your recruitment profile. You’ll deliver a keynote speech and present your career opportunities. Ongoing and by appointment Career Trek - We’ll bring a group of up to 25 students who are a good fit for your company to your location. You’ll present your career opportunities on-site and show students and recent graduates their future workplace. Ongoing and by appointment Every Friday online or at Hansa Haus Munich AI Academy for students. If you’re interested in an exciting topic related to the use of AI, then this program is perfect for you. Ongoing and by appointment Every Friday online or at Hansa Haus Munich Q4 Internship: Flash / Business Cases Event checklists FAQs for companies LMU Career Forum - 22.05.2026 The venue is the Kardinal Wendel Haus in Munich , near Münchner Freiheit. The event opens for students at 10:00 a.m. We will be on site for you starting around 9:00 a.m. Please set up your booths between 9:00 and 10:00 a.m. Please have your promotional materials delivered the day before the event and picked up again at the end of the day (5:00 PM – 6:00 PM). Please make sure to label your materials clearly! Catering Schedule Starting at 9:00 AM Welcome coffee and pretzels for company representatives Starting at 10:00 AM Check-in opens and welcome coffee for students 12:00 PM – 1:30 PM Networking buffet for company representatives and students 2:30 PM Coffee and pastries 4:00 PM End of the event You will need one to two roll-up banners and giveaways for approximately 200 students. Students participate on a “hop-on-hop-off” basis. This means that, as expected, there will be a steady flow of visitors throughout the day. Ideally, you should have 2–3 colleagues on site. An exhibition booth is not required. We will provide you with two tables where you can interact with interested students and display promotional materials. Wi-Fi and electricity are available on-site (for your company’s booth; no password required) The dress code for students is open / casual / smart / business casual Students will wear name tags . We generally recommend traveling by public transportation (Münchner Freiheit subway station). Unfortunately, following a decision by the LHST, we cannot provide you with parking passes. There are three parking garages in the immediate vicinity available to you. The event will be documented by our photographer , Sabine Jakobs. Feel free to ask her if she can take a photo of you and your team on-site. Regardless of this, we will try to ensure that every company is featured in one or more photos. We will prepare name tags and LinkedIn profiles for you. Please send us the names, job titles, and LinkedIn links of all participants by 15.05. at the latest ! Shape Your Career! Consulting & MINT am 27.03.2026 Shape Your Career! Consulting & MINT Veranstaltungsort der Messe ist das Literaturhaus München , 3.OG Die Veranstaltung wird um 10:00 Uhr für die Studierenden eröffnet. Wir sind ab 9:00 Uhr für Sie vor Ort. Sie können Rollups / Werbematerial am Vorabend anliefern lassen. Idealerweise aber bringen Sie diese am selben Tag mit und nehmen diese am Abend wieder mit. Bitte achten Sie unbedingt auf ausreichende Beschriftung. Sie benötigen ein bis zwei Rollups und Give Aways für ca. 150 Studierende. Ein Messestand wird nicht benötigt. Sie erhalten einen Tisch von uns, an dem Sie sich mit Interessent/-innen austauschen können und an dem Sie Werbematerial auslegen können. Es gibt vor Ort WiFi und Strom (für Ihren Unternehmensstand). Der Dresscode der Studierenden ist open / casual / smart casual. Die Studierenden tragen Namensschilder. Sie erhalten am Montag vor dem Event die Liste der vorangemeldeten Studierenden und deren CVs. Die CVs können Sie bis zu vier Wochen nach dem Event für Recruiting-Zwecke weiter verwenden, wenn Sie im Einzelfall den Recruiting-Prozess fortsetzen natürlich gemäß Ihren eigenen Datenschutzbestimmungen länger. Wir stellen Ihnen Namensschilder zur Verfügung. Bitte senden Sie bis spätestens 5 Werktage vor dem Event per Email, wer aus Ihrem Unternehmen das Event besuchen und begleiten wird , so dass wir die Namensschilder und Tischunterlagen für Sie erstellen können (LinkedIn-Profile zum Vernetzen). Die Veranstaltung wird von unserer Profifotografin Sabine Jakobs dokumentiert. Sie können sie gerne ansprechen, ob Sie ein Foto von Ihnen und Ihrem Team vor Ort macht. Wir versuchen unabhängig davon, dass jedes Unternehmen auf einem oder mehreren Fotos zu sehen ist. Ablaufplan ab 10:00 Check-In für Studierende 10:00 - 16:00 Messe, Einzelgespräche, Networking, Key-Notes 12:00 - 13:30 Networking Buffet ca. 16 Uhr Ende der Veranstaltung Career Trek Veranstaltungsort ist Ihr Unternehmensstandort. Bitte teilen Sie uns rechtzeitig mit, wo wir uns bei Ihnen treffen. Ihnen steht ein Zeitfenster zur freien Gestaltung von 10:00 - 14:00 zur Verfügung, ein Muster-Ablauf wäre 10:00 Uhr Begrüßung (mit Kaffee) 10:15 Präsentation und oder Rundgang durch das Unternehmen 12:30 Business & Networking Lunch 13:30 Verabschiedung Der Dresscode der Studierenden ist open / casual / smart casual Die Gruppengröße wird idR zwischen 10 und 25 Studierenden sein. Sie erhalten einige Tage im Vorfeld die CVs der Besucher:innen. Die CVs können Sie bis zu vier Wochen nach dem Event für Recruiting-Zwecke weiter verwenden, wenn Sie im Einzelfall den Recruiting-Prozess fortsetzen natürlich gemäß Ihren eigenen Datenschutzbestimmungen länger. Es wäre klasse, wen die Studierenden bei Ihnen vor Ort Personen auf senior, junior und intern Level kennenlernen. Meet & Greet Veranstaltungsort ist das Hansa Haus München , Brienner Str. 39. Das Event beginnt um 18:00 und endet um 20:00. Wir sind ab 17:30 für Sie vor Ort. Rechnen Sie mit 20 - 30 Studierenden, deren CVs Sie im Vorfeld von uns erhalten. Idealerweise besteht Ihr Team vor Ort nicht nur aus senior Mitarbeiter:innen sondern gerne auch aus Fresh(wo:)men, Praktikant:innen und/oder Werkstudent:innen. Für die Unternehmensvorstellung mit anschließender Fragerunde empfehlen wir die erste Stunde. Seien Sie bei dieser möglichst konkret und geben direkte Einblicke in Ihre Arbeit und in Ihren Recruitingprozess. Als Werbematerial reichen zwei Rollups und einige Give Aways aus. Präsentationstechnik ist vor Ort vorhanden. In der zweiten Stunde laden wir Sie und die Studierenden zu einem kleinen Networking Snack ein. Es gibt keinen festen Dresscode. Wir schließen das Event um 20:00 Uhr. Sie können dann das Networking noch bis ca. 20:30 ausklingen lassen. Q4 Internship Flash 2025 - Abschluss-Event am 05.12.2025 Zunächst einmal vielen Dank für all die spannenden Cases im Laufe des Jahres. Wir freuen uns sehr auf das große Abschluss-Messe mit Ihnen allen im Kardinal-Wendel-Haus. Wann: FR 05.12.2025 von 10 - 16 Uhr Eingeladen sind neben den Studierenden, die an den Cases teilgenommen haben, auch andere interessierte Studierende. Diese wollen wir gemeinsam mit Ihnen für das Event kommendes Jahr gewinnen. Ich würde mich sehr freuen, wenn Sie wieder dabei sind in 2026. Das Format der übers Jahr verteilten Cases hat sich bewährt. Bitte füllen Sie zur Teilnahme diesen Bogen aus. Nachfolgend finden Sie die FAQs zur Abschlussmesse. Ort: Kardinal-Wendel-Haus, Mandlstr. 23, München. Wir empfehlen die Anreise mit öffentlichen Verkehrsmitteln. Leider gibt es keine Parkausweise der LHST München mehr. Messematerial: Dieses können Sie am Vorabend ans Veranstaltungshaus senden: Kardinal-Wendel-Haus, Mandlstr. 23, 80802 München, für Messe LMU, zHd. Frau Grünwald. Bitte lassen Sie das Material am Abend des Events wieder abholen (17:00 - 20:00 Uhr). Bei den Giveaways: Rechnen Sie mit 100 - 250 Studierenden, die über den Tag verteilt die Messe besuchen. Sie erhalten wie immer die CVs am Montag vor der Messe. Wir empfehlen unbedingt, die Studierenden persönlich anzuschreiben, deren Profil besonders spannend für Sie ist. z.B.: \"Hallo, schön, dass Du zum Q4 Abschluss Event kommst. Dein Profil könnte zu uns passen. Besuch uns doch an unserem Stand. Wir freuen uns auf Dich.\" - Das erhöht die Verbindlichkeit bei diesem für Studierende kostenfreien Event signifikant. Wir freuen uns sehr auf das Event mit Ihnen. Bei Fragen schreiben Sie uns gerne oder stellen uns einen Calendly / Zoom Termin ein. International Event Working here & abroad - 24.10.2025 Veranstaltungsort: Literaturhaus München, 3. OG ( Salvatorplatz 1, 80333 München ) Die Vormittags-Veranstaltung (zwei Bewerbungs-Workshops) wird um 09:00 Uhr eröffnet. Wir sind ab 08:30 vor Ort. Sie können ab 11:00 für den Messeteil anreisen. Ab 11:30 Uhr gibt es einen Business-Lunch , zu dem Sie herzlich eingeladen sind. Die Messe beginnt um 12:00 Uhr. Sie können Rollups / Werbematerial am Vorabend anliefern lassen (Adresse siehe oben, Ansprechpartnerin vor Ort ist Carolin Frohnauer). Kalkulieren Sie bei Ihrem Werbematerial mit ca. 150 - 200 Studierenden. Ein Messestand wird nicht benötigt. Wir stellen Ihnen Tische und Stühle zur Verfügung. Hier können Sie sich mit Interessentinnen und Interessenten austauschen und Ihr Werbematerial auslegen. Bringen Sie gern bis zu zwei Roll-Ups mit. Der Dresscode der Studierenden ist casual / smart casual. Die Studierenden tragen Namensschilder . Wir werden auch für Sie Namensschilder erstellen. Ebenso bekommen Sie als Unternehmen eine Karte , auf der sich Codes zu Ihren LinkedIn-Profilen befinden, sodass sich Studierende möglichst einfach mit Ihnen verknüpfen können. Legen Sie diese am besten auf Ihrem Tisch aus. Wir empfehlen, mit etwa drei Unternehmensvertreterinnen anzureisen. Hier ist eine Mischung aus HR-Mitarbeitenden sowie Mitarbeitenden aus den Fachbereichen ideal. Wir empfehlen die Anreise mit öffentlichen Verkehrsmitteln . Der Odeonsplatz ist fußläufig 5 Minuten entfernt. Wenige Tage vor dem Event erhalten Sie von uns die Liste mit den Studierenden , die sich für das Event vorangemeldet haben. Sie erhalten zudem die CVs . Wir erwarten am Veranstaltungstag selbst zudem einige spontane Besucherinnen und Besucher. Die Veranstaltung wird von unserer Fotografin Sabine Jakobs dokumentiert. Sie können sie gerne ansprechen, ob sie ein Foto von Ihnen macht. Wir versuchen unabhängig davon, dass jedes Unternehmen auf einem oder mehreren Fotos zu sehen ist. Ihre To-Do's: Bitte teilen Sie uns bis spätestens 19.10 mit, wer aus Ihrem Unternehmen an der Messe teilnehmen wird. Wir benötigen folgende Informationen: Name, Vorname, Positionsbezeichnung, ggf. LinkedIn-Kontakt Bitte teilen Sie uns baldmöglichst mit, welche Studierenden Sie ansprechen möchten ( Studiengang / Fachbereich ). Bewerbung Ihrer eigenen Events Hier können Sie Ihre eigenen Events bewerben. Guidelines of the LMU Career Services Empowerment and Potential Development The focus of our daily work lies in supporting our students in the best possible way on their path toward professional life. We deliberately adopt a strengths-oriented approach and foster the individual potential of our students. Through our broad range of services, we aim to empower students to explore the wide variety of career opportunities, to find their own path in the professional world, and to gain a deeper understanding of themselves and their aspirations. Promotion of Innovation In order to provide optimal support to our students and partners, we regularly integrate current formats, discussions, and impulses into our services. Innovation, openness, and creativity - combined with an awareness of the needs of our target groups - enable us to provide contemporary Career Services, both in person and digitally. Promotion of Diversity As a university with a wide range of disciplines, we experience the added value of interdisciplinary exchange every day. Therefore, our events are generally open to all fields of study. For our partners, interests, skills, and the recruitment of successful new employees do not end at disciplinary boundaries. In addition, we promote our career events in close coordination with our partners and inform students about the primary target groups. Beyond disciplinary diversity, our work is also shaped by the diversity of our students. It is particularly important to us to make our services equally accessible to all LMU Munich students and to promote equal opportunities. The internationalization of universities is an integral part of our services. International students at LMU are a natural part of all our events. Furthermore, through the scholarship programs we administer, we support students in undertaking international internships around the world. Partnership and Exchange Our work is based on a relationship of mutual respect with our students and partners. Mutual trust, transparency, and openness to the unique conditions of the university environment are essential. In addition, we actively promote direct exchange between our various target groups. Your contact for all of LMU's Career Events & Fairs Dr.phil. Stephan Pflaum LMU's Career Services Consultant Career Events & Services / Deputy Head of Career Service Send an email Zoom appointment for employers More Johanna Uitz, M.A. LMU's Career Services Consultant for Internationalization & Employability / project manager FIT-LMU International Careers, Events & Seminars, Mentoring, Employer Services Send an email More Please read our terms & conditions . up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close Schließen"
